2 into its prime factors and then simplify the square root based on those factors.\n\nFirst, let's factorize 242:\n- \\(242 \\div 2 = 121\\)\n- \\(121 = 11^2\\)\n\nSo, \\(242 = 2 \\times 11^2\\).\n\nNow, we can simplify \\(\\sqrt{242}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{242} = \\sqrt{2 \\times 11^2} = \\sqrt{2} \\times \\sqrt{11^2} = 11\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the square root of 242\nsqrt_242 = math.sqrt(242)\n\n# Simplify the square root by factorizing 242\nfactorized_sqrt = 11 * math.sqrt(2)\n\nprint((sqrt_242, factorized_sqrt))\n```\n```output\n(15.556349186104045, 15.556349186104046)\n```\nThe calculated value of \\(\\sqrt{242}\\) is approximately 15.556349186104045, and the simplified form \\(11\\sqrt{2}\\) also evaluates to approximately 15.556349186104046. This confirms that the simplified form is correct.\n\nSo, the simplified form of \\(\\sqrt{242}\\) is \\(\\boxed{11\\sqrt{2}}\\).", "To simplify \\(\\sqrt{242}\\), we need to factorize 242 into its prime factors and simplify the square root based on those factors. Let's go through the steps:\n\n1. Factorize 242 into its prime factors.\n2. Simplify the square root by taking out any perfect squares.\n\nLet's start by factorizing 242. We can do this by checking for divisibility by prime numbers.\n\n- 242 is divisible by 2: \\(242 \\div 2 = 121\\).\n- 121 is divisible by 11: \\(121 \\div 11 = 11\\).\n- 11 is a prime number.\n\nSo, the prime factorization of 242 is \\(2 \\times 11 \\times 11\\).\n\nNow we can simplify the square root:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{242} = \\sqrt{2 \\times 11 \\times 11} = \\sqrt{11^2 \\times 2} = 11\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this using Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Original number\nnumber = 242\n\n# Factorize the number and simplify the square root\nsqrt_number = math.sqrt(number)\nsimplified_sqrt = int(math.sqrt(number // (number // math.sqrt(number)**2)))\n\nprint((sqrt_number, simplified_sqrt))\n```\n```output\n(15.5563491861