bine these terms, we need a common denominator. The common denominator for \\(\\cos x \\sin x\\) and \\(\\cos x\\) is \\(\\cos x \\sin x\\). So we rewrite the second term with the common denominator:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{\\sin x \\cdot \\sin x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} = \\frac{\\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x}.\n\\]\n\nNow the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x} = \\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x}.\n\\]\n\n4. Recall the Pythagorean identity: \\(1 - \\sin^2 x = \\cos^2 x\\). So the expression simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\cos^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x} = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\cot x.\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified form of the given expression is \\(\\cot x\\).\n\nLet's verify this using Python code to ensure the accuracy of our result.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, sec, sin, cos, simplify, cot\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the expression\r\nexpression = sec(x) / sin(x) - sin(x) / cos(x)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = simplify(expression)\r\n\r\n# Display the simplified expression\r\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```\n```output\n1/tan(x)\n```\nThe simplified expression \\(\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\) is indeed \\(\\cot x\\), which is equivalent to \\(\\frac{1}{\\tan x}\\).\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\cot x}\n\\]", "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Express \\(\\sec x\\) in terms of \\(\\cos x\\). Recall that \\(\\sec x = \\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\).\n2. Substitute \\(\\sec x\\) in the expression.\n3. Simplify the resulting expression.\n\nLet's do this step-by-step:\n\n1. Substitute \\(\\sec x = \\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\) into the expression:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\cos x}}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}