$, which is equal to $1.5$. When Remmy multiplies $10$ by $1.5$, he gets $15$. Therefore, the number by which Remmy should multiply $10$ is $\\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}$.", 'The answer is $15$.  We know that dividing by a fraction is the same as multiplying by the reciprocal of that fraction.  So, we can rewrite the problem as $10 \\cdot \\frac{3}{2}$.  We can simplify this to $\\frac{30}{2}$, which equals $15$.  Therefore, the answer is $\\boxed{15}$.', 'To divide by a fraction, we multiply by its reciprocal. The reciprocal of $\\frac{2}{3}$ is $\\frac{3}{2}$. Therefore, Remmy should multiply $10$ by $\\frac{3}{2}$. The answer is $\\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}$.', 'The reciprocal of $\\frac{2}{3}$ is $\\frac{3}{2}$.  Therefore, Remmy should multiply $10$ by $\\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}$ to get the answer.', '$\\frac{2}{3}$ of what number is $8$?  \\boxed{}. \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{ 