uad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\quad \\text{  } \\', 'What is the area of a square with a side length of $25$?\n $$\\text{(A)}\\ 25 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 50 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 625 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 1000 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 1250$$\n 2021 AMC 10A Problem 1.png\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.igidBody\n 1. What is the value of $x$ if $x + 3 = 7$?\n \n Step-by-step reasoning:\n \n To find the value of \\( x \\), we need to isolate \\( x \\) on one side of the equation. We can do this by subtracting 3 from both sides of the equation.\n \n \\[\n x + 3 - 3 = 7 - 3\n \\]\n \n Simplifying both sides, we get:\n \n \\[\n x = 4\n \\]\n \n So, the value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).\n\n2. What is the value of \\( y \\) if \\( 2y - 5 = 11 \\)?\n\n Step-by-step reasoning:\n\n To find the value of \\( y \\), we need to isolate \\( y \\) on one side of the equation. We can do this in two steps. First, we add 5 to both sides of the equation.\n \n \\[\n 2y - 5 + 5 = 11 + 5\n \\]\n \n Simplifying both sides, we get:\n \n \\[\n 2y = 16\n \\]\n \n Next, we divide both sides by 2 to solve for \\( y \\).\n \n \\[\n \\frac{2y}{2} = \\frac{16}{2}\n \\]\n \n Simplifying both sides, we get:\n \n \\[\n y = 8\n \\]\n \n So, the value of \\( y \\) is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).\n\n3. What is the value of \\( z \\) if \\( 3z + 4 = 19 \\)?\n\n Step-by-step reasoning:\n\n To find the value of \\( z \\), we need to isolate \\( z \\) on one side of the equation. We can do this in two steps. First, we subtract 4 from both sides of the equation.\n \n \\[\n 3z + 4 - 4 = 19 - 4\n \\]\n \n Simplifying both sides, we get:\n \n \\[\n 3z = 15\n \\]\n \n Next, we divide both sides by 3 to solve for \\( z \\).\n \n \\[\n \\frac{3z}{3} = \\frac{15}{3}\n \\]\n \n Simplifying both sides, we get:\n \n \\[\n z = 5\n \\]\n \n So, the value of \\( z \\) is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).\n\n4. What is the value of \\( w \\) if \\( 5w - 7 = 13 \\)?\n\n Step-by-step reasoning:\n\n To find the value of \\( w \\), we need to isolate \\( w \\) on one side of the equation. We can do this in two steps. First, we add 7 to both sides of the equation.\n \n \\[\n 5w - 7 + 7 = 13 + 7\n \\]\n \n Simplifying both sides, we get:\n \n \\[\n 5w = 20\n \\]\n \n Next, we divide both sides by 5 to solve for \\( w \\).\n \n \\[\n \\frac{5w}{5} = \\frac{20}{5}\n \\]\n \n Simplifying both sides, we get:\n \n \\[\n w = 4\n \\]\n \n So, the value of \\( w \\) is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).\n\n5. What is the value of \\( v \\) if \\( 4v + 6 = 22 \\)?\n\n Step-by-step reasoning:\n\n To find the value of \\( v \\), we need to isolate \\( v \\) on one side of the equation. We can do this in two steps. First, we subtract 6 from both sides of the equation.\n \n \\[\n 4v + 6 - 6 = 22 - 6\n \\]\n \n Simplifying both sides, we get:\n \n \\[\n 4v = 16\n \\]\n \n Next, we divide both sides by 4 to solve for \\( v \\).\n \n \\[\n \\frac{4v}{4} = \\frac{16}{4}\n \\]\n \n Simplifying both sides, we get:\n \n \\[\n v = 4\n \\]\n \n So, the value of \\( v \\) is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).\n\n6. What is the value of \\( u \\) if \\( 6u - 8 = 20 \\)?\n\n Step-by-step reasoning:\n\n To find the value of \\( u \\), we need to isolate \\( u \\) on one side of the equation. We can do this in two steps. First, we add 8 to both sides of the equation.\n \n \\[\n 6u - 8 + 8 = 20 +