n that \\( \\angle BAD = 110^\\circ \\) and \\( \\angle CDA = 100^\\circ \\). Therefore:\n   - \\( 3x = 110^\\circ \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{110^\\circ}{3} \\)\n   - \\( 3y = 100^\\circ \\Rightarrow y = \\frac{100^\\circ}{3} \\)\n\n4. Now, let's find \\( \\angle AFD \\). Notice that \\( \\angle AFD \\) is an external angle to \\( \\triangle AFD \\). The measure of an external angle of a triangle is equal to the sum of the measures of the two opposite interior angles. So:\n   - \\( \\angle AFD = \\angle DAF + \\angle ADE \\)\n   - \\( \\angle AFD = x + y \\)\n   - \\( \\angle AFD = \\frac{110^\\circ}{3} + \\frac{100^\\circ}{3} = \\frac{210^\\circ}{3} = 70^\\circ \\)\n\nSo, the measure of \\( \\angle AFD \\) is \\( 70^\\circ \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given angles\nangle_BAD = 110\nangle_CDA = 100\n\n# Trisected angles\nx = angle_BAD / 3\ny = angle_CDA / 3\n\n# Angle AFD is the sum of x and y\nangle_AFD = x + y\nprint(angle_AFD)\n```\n```output\n70.0\n```\nThe measure of \\( \\angle AFD \\) is \\(\\boxed{70^\\circ}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to use the properties of angle trisection and the sum of angles in a quadrilateral.\n\n1. Let's denote the trisected angles as follows:\n   - Angle \\( \\angle BAD = 3x \\)\n   - Angle \\( \\angle CDA = 3y \\)\n\n2. Since \\( \\angle BAD \\) and \\( \\angle CDA \\) are trisected, we have:\n   - \\( \\angle BAE = \\angle EAF = \\angle FAD = x \\)\n   - \\( \\angle FAD = \\angle ADF = \\angle FDC = y \\)\n\n3. The sum of the interior angles of quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\) is \\(360^\\circ\\). Therefore:\n   \\[\n   \\angle BAD + \\angle ABC + \\angle BCD + \\angle CDA = 360^\\circ\n   \\]\n   Substituting the trisected angles, we get:\n   \\[\n   3x + \\angle ABC + \\angle BCD + 3y = 360^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n4. We are given that \\( \\angle ABC = 110^\\circ \\) and \\( \\angle BCD = 100^\\circ \\). Substituting these values, we get:\n   \\[\n   3x + 110^\\circ + 100^\\circ + 3y = 