s 85^\\circ] = \\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nNext, let's simplify the denominator:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nUsing the product-to-sum identities:\n\\[\n\\sin A \\cos B = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin (A+B) + \\sin (A-B)],\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos A \\sin B = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin (A+B) - \\sin (A-B)].\n\\]\n\nWe can rewrite the terms:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) + \\sin (5^\\circ - 20^\\circ)] = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 25^\\circ + \\sin (-15^\\circ)] = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ],\n\\]\n\\[\n-\\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ = -\\frac{1}{2} [\\sin (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) + \\sin (35^\\circ - 50^\\circ)] = -\\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 85^\\circ + \\sin (-15^\\circ)] = -\\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 85^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ],\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) - \\sin (5^\\circ - 20^\\circ)] = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin (-15^\\circ)] = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 25^\\circ + \\sin 15^\\circ],\n\\]\n\\[\n-\\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = -\\frac{1}{2} [\\sin (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) - \\sin (35^\\circ - 50^\\circ)] = -\\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 85^\\circ - \\sin (-15^\\circ)] = -\\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 85^\\circ + \\sin 15^\\circ].\n\\]\n\nCombining these, the denominator becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ] - \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 85^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ] + \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 25^\\circ + \\sin 15^\\circ] - \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 85^\\circ + \\sin 15^\\circ].\n\\]\n\nSimplifying further:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ + \\sin 15^\\circ + \\sin 25^\\circ + \\sin 15^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ] = \\frac{1}{2} [2\\sin 25^\\circ - 2\\sin 85^\\circ] = \\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ}.\n\\]\n\nWe can use the sum-to-product identities:\n\\[\n\\cos A + \\cos B = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right),\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin A - \\sin B = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right).\n\\]\n\nApplying these identities, we get:\n\\[\n\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos (-30^\\circ) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin (-30^\\circ) = -2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ}{-2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 30^\\circ}{-\\sin 30^\\circ} = \\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}{-\\frac{1}{2}} = -\\sqrt{3}.\n\\]\n\nThus, $\\theta = 120^\\circ$ since $\\tan 120^\\circ = -\\sqrt{3}$. The least positive angle $\\theta$ is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{120}.\n\\]", "To solve the given problem, we need to simplify the expression for $\\tan \\theta$ and then find the corresponding angle $\\theta$.\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}{\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nWe can use trigonometric identities to simplify the numerator and the denominator. Recall the angle addition and subtraction formulas:\n\\[\n\\cos A \\cos B - \\sin A \\sin B = \\cos (A + B)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin A \\cos B + \\cos A \\sin B = \\sin (A + B)\n\\]\n\nLet's simplify the numerator and the denominator step by step.\n\n### Simplifying the Numerator\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\cos (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) = \\cos 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = \\cos (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\cos 85^\\circ\n\\]\nSo the numerator becomes:\n\\[\n\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ\n\\]\n\n### Simplifying the Denominator\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\sin (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) = \\sin 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n-\\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = -(\\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ) = -\\sin (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = -\\sin 85^\\circ\n\\]\nSo the denominator becomes:\n\\[\n\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression for $\\tan \\theta$ becomes:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nWe can use the sum-to-product identities:\n\\[\n\\cos A + \\cos B = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin A - \\sin B = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)\n\\]\n\nApplying these identities:\n\\[\n\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos (-30^\\circ) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin (-30^\\circ) = -2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ\n\\]\n\nSo the expression for $\\tan \\theta$ becomes:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ}{-2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 30^\\circ}{-\\sin 30^\\circ} = \\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}{-\\frac{1}{2}} = -\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, $\\tan \\theta = -\\sqrt{3}$. The least positive angle $\\theta$ for which $\\tan \\theta = -\\sqrt{3}$ is $150^\\circ$ (since $\\tan 150^\\circ = -\\sqrt{3}$).\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{150}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the accuracy of the result.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given expression for tan(theta)\ndef tan_theta():\n    numerator = math.cos(math.radians(5)) * math.cos(math.radians(20)) + math.cos(math.radians(35)) * math.cos(math.radians(50)) - math.sin(math.radians(5)) * math.sin(math.radians(20)) - math.sin(math.radians(35)) * math.sin(math.radians(50))\n    denominator = math.sin(math.radians(5)) * math.cos(math.radians(20)) - math.sin(math.radians(35)) * math.cos(math.radians(50)) + math.cos(math.radians(5)) * math.sin(math.radians(20)) - math.cos(math.radians(35)) * math.sin(math.radians(50))\n    return numerator / denominator\n\n# Calculate the angle theta\ntan_value = tan_theta()\ntheta = math.degrees(math.atan(tan_value))\n# Ensure theta is the least positive angle\nif theta < 0:\n    theta += 180\n\nprint(theta)\n```", "To solve the given problem, we need to simplify the expression for $\\tan \\theta$ and then find the angle $\\theta$.\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}{\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}.\n\\]\n\nWe can use trigonometric identities to simplify the numerator and the denominator.\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the numerator and the denominator using the angle addition and subtraction formulas:\n\nNumerator:\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ.\n\\]\nUsing the identity $\\cos A \\cos B - \\sin A \\sin B = \\cos (A + B)$, we get:\n\\[\n\\cos (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) + \\cos (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nDenominator:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ.\n\\]\nUsing the identity $\\sin A \\cos B + \\cos A \\sin B = \\sin (A + B)$, we get:\n\\[\n\\sin (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) - \\sin (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nSo, the expression for $\\tan \\theta$ simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the identity $\\cos A + \\cos B = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)$ for the numerator, and $\\sin A - \\sin B = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)$ for the denominator:\n\\[\n\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos (-30^\\circ) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin (-30^\\circ) = -2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression for $\\tan \\theta$ becomes:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ}{-2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 30^\\circ}{-\\sin 30^\\circ} = \\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}{-\\frac{1}{2}} = -\\sqrt{3}.\n\\]\n\nSo, $\\tan \\theta = -\\sqrt{3}$. The least positive angle $\\theta$ for which $\\tan \\theta = -\\sqrt{3}$ is $120^\\circ$ (since $\\tan 120^\\circ = -\\sqrt{3}$).\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{120}\n\\]", "To solve for the least positive angle $\\theta$ such that\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}{\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ},\n\\]\nwe need to simplify the expression on the right-hand side.\n\nFirst, we recognize that the numerator and the denominator can be simplified using trigonometric identities. Specifically, we can use the angle addition and subtraction formulas:\n\\[\n\\cos A \\cos B - \\sin A \\sin B = \\cos (A + B),\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin A \\cos B + \\cos A \\sin B = \\sin (A + B).\n\\]\n\nLet's rewrite the numerator and the denominator using these identities:\n\\[\n\\text{Numerator} = \\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = \\cos (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) + \\cos (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ.\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Denominator} = \\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = \\sin (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) - \\sin (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nNow, we can use the identity for the sum and difference of sines and cosines:\n\\[\n\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos (-30^\\circ) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\sqrt{3} \\cos 55^\\circ.\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin (-30^\\circ) = -2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ = -2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = -\\cos 55^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\cos 55^\\circ}{-\\cos 55^\\circ} = -\\sqrt{3}.\n\\]\n\nWe know that $\\tan \\theta = -\\sqrt{3}$ corresponds to an angle in the second or fourth quadrant. The least positive angle $\\theta$ that satisfies this equation is $120^\\circ$ (since $\\tan 120^\\circ = -\\sqrt{3}$).\n\nSo, the least positive angle $\\theta$ is $\\boxed{120}$ degrees.", "To solve this problem, we need to simplify the given expression for $\\tan \\theta$ and then find the angle $\\theta$ that satisfies this expression. Let's break down the problem into manageable steps and use Python with the sympy library to solve it.\n\n1. **Simplify the Numerator and Denominator:**\n   The given expression for $\\tan \\theta$ is:\n   \\[\n   \\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}{\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}.\n   \\]\n   We can use trigonometric identities to simplify the numerator and the denominator.\n\n2. **Use Trigonometric Identities:**\n   We can use the product-to-sum identities and the angle addition formulas to simplify the expression. Let's start by simplifying the numerator and the denominator separately.\n\n3. **Simplify the Expression:**\n   We can use sympy to handle the trigonometric simplification and then find the angle $\\theta$.\n\nLet's implement this in Python using sympy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the angle in degrees\nangle_5 = sp.rad(5)\nangle_20 = sp.rad(20)\nangle_35 = sp.rad(35)\nangle_50 = sp.rad(50)\n\n# Define the trigonometric expressions\nnumerator = sp.cos(angle_5) * sp.cos(angle_20) + sp.cos(angle_35) * sp.cos(angle_50) - sp.sin(angle_5) * sp.sin(angle_20) - sp.sin(angle_35) * sp.sin(angle_50)\ndenominator = sp.sin(angle_5) * sp.cos(angle_20) - sp.sin(angle_35) * sp.cos(angle_50) + sp.cos(angle_5) * sp.sin(angle_20) - sp.cos(angle_35) * sp.sin(angle_50)\n\n# Simplify the expression for tan(theta)\ntan_theta = numerator / denominator\ntan_theta_simplified = sp.simplify(tan_theta)\n\n# Find the angle theta in degrees\ntheta = sp.atan(tan_theta_simplified)\ntheta_degrees = sp.deg(theta)\n\n# Convert the angle to the least positive angle\ntheta_degrees = sp.Mod(theta_degrees, 360)\n\nprint(theta_degrees)\n```\n```output\n180*atan((sqrt(2)*cos(7*pi/36) - 2*sin(pi/36))/(sqrt(2)*sin(7*pi/36) + 2*cos(pi/36)))/pi\n```\nThe output we received is a symbolic expression for the angle $\\theta$ in terms of trigonometric functions. To find the numerical value of this expression, we can evaluate it using sympy's `evalf` method.\n\nLet's modify the code to evaluate the expression numerically.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the angle in degrees\nangle_5 = sp.rad(5)\nangle_20 = sp.rad(20)\nangle_35 = sp.rad(35)\nangle_50 = sp.rad(50)\n\n# Define the trigonometric expressions\nnumerator = sp.cos(angle_5) * sp.cos(angle_20) + sp.cos(angle_35) * sp.cos(angle_50) - sp.sin(angle_5) * sp.sin(angle_20) - sp.sin(angle_35) * sp.sin(angle_50)\ndenominator = sp.sin(angle_5) * sp.cos(angle_20) - sp.sin(angle_35) * sp.cos(angle_50) + sp.cos(angle_5) * sp.sin(angle_20) - sp.cos(angle_35) * sp.sin(angle_50)\n\n# Simplify the expression for tan(theta)\ntan_theta = numerator / denominator\ntan_theta_simplified = sp.simplify(tan_theta)\n\n# Find the angle theta in degrees\ntheta = sp.atan(tan_theta_simplified)\ntheta_degrees = sp.deg(theta)\n\n# Convert the angle to the least positive angle\ntheta_degrees = sp.Mod(theta_degrees, 360)\n\n# Evaluate the angle numerically\ntheta_degrees_evaluated = theta_degrees.evalf()\n\nprint(theta_degrees_evaluated)\n```\n```output\n15.0000000000000\n```\nThe numerical value of the least positive angle $\\theta$ that satisfies the given expression is $\\boxed{15^\\circ}$.", "To solve this problem, we need to carefully analyze the properties of the sequence \\(a_n\\). The sequence has the property that for every positive integer \\(k\\), the subsequence \\(a_{2k-1}, a_{2k}, a_{2k+1}\\) is geometric, and the subsequence \\(a_{2k}, a_{2k+1}, a_{2k+2}\\) is arithmetic. This gives us two key relationships:\n\n1.