ose 3 boys out of 7 and 2 girls out of 4. This is a combinatorial problem where the order of selection does not matter, so we can use the binomial coefficient formula:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nThe number of ways to choose 3 boys out of 7 is given by \\(\\binom{7}{3}\\), and the number of ways to choose 2 girls out of 4 is given by \\(\\binom{4}{2}\\). The total number of ways to choose 3 boys and 2 girls is the product of these two values:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{7}{3} \\times \\binom{4}{2}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this step by step using Python.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the binomial coefficient for choosing 3 boys out of 7\nboys_combinations = math.comb(7, 3)\n\n# Calculate the binomial coefficient for choosing 2 girls out of 4\ngirls_combinations = math.comb(4, 2)\n\n# The total number of ways to choose 3 boys and 2 girls\ntotal_combinations = boys_combinations * girls_combinations\nprint(total_combinations)\n```\n```output\n210\n```\nThe total number of ways Mr. Brennan can pick 3 boys and 2 girls to give a group presentation tomorrow is \\(\\boxed{210}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to determine the number of ways to choose 3 boys out of 7 and 2 girls out of 4. The order in which the boys and girls are chosen does not matter, so we will use combinations.\n\nThe number of ways to choose 3 boys out of 7 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{7}{3} \\), and the number of ways to choose 2 girls out of 4 is given by \\( \\binom{4}{2} \\). The total number of ways to choose the group is the product of these two combinations.\n\nThe combination formula is given by:\n\\[ \\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \\]\n\nFirst, we calculate \\( \\binom{7}{3} \\):\n\\[ \\binom{7}{3} = \\frac{7!}{3!(7-3)!} = \\frac{7!}{3!4!} = \\frac{7 \\times 6 \\times 5}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = 35 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( \\binom{4}{2} \\):\n\\[ \\binom{4}{2} = \\frac{4!}{2!(4-2)!} = \\frac{4!}{2!2!} = \\frac{4 \\times 3}{2 \\times 1} = 6 \