s using Python code.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base_n(decimal_number, base):\n    if decimal_number == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while decimal_number:\n        digits.append(int(decimal_number % base))\n        decimal_number //= base\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_representation = decimal_to_base_n(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_5_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base $5$ representation of $555_{10}$ is $\\boxed{4210_5}$.', 'To convert a number from base 10 to base 5, we repeatedly divide the number by 5 and keep track of the remainders. The conversion process involves the following steps:\n\n1. Divide the number by 5.\n2. Record the remainder.\n3. Update the number to the quotient from the division.\n4. Repeat steps 1-3 until the quotient is 0.\n5. The base 5 representation is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.\n\nLet\'s perform this conversion using Python code.\n```python\ndef convert_to_base_5(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    \n    base_5_digits = []\n    \n    while n > 0:\n        remainder = n % 5\n        base_5_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        n = n // 5\n    \n    # The base 5 representation is the reverse of the collected remainders\n    base_5_digits.reverse()\n    return \'\'.join(base_5_digits)\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\nbase_5_representation = convert_to_base_5(555)\nprint(base_5_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base 5 representation of the number \\(555_{10}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\).', 'To express the decimal number \\(555_{10}\\) in base \\(5\\), we need to repeatedly divide the number by \\(5\\) and keep track of the remainders. The remainders, read in reverse order, will give us the base \\(5\\) representation of the number.\n\nHere is the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Divide \\(555\\) by \\(5\\), which gives a quotient of \\(111\\) and a remainder of \\(0\\).\n2. Divide \\(111\\) by \\(5\\), which gives a quotient of \\(22\\) and a remainder of \\(1\\).\n3. Divide \\(22\\) by \\(5\\), which gives a quotient of \\(4\\) and a remainder of \\(2\\).\n4. Divide \\(4\\) by \\(5\\), which gives a quotient of \\(0\\) and a remainder of \\(4\\).\n\nThe remainders, read in reverse order, give us the base \\(5\\) representation of \\(555_{10}\\). So, \\(555_{10} = 4210_5\\).\n\nLet\'s confirm this by implementing the process in Python.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base_n(decimal_number, base):\n    if decimal_number == 0:\n        return "0"\n    \n    digits = []\n    while decimal_number:\n        digits.append(int(decimal_number % base))\n        decimal_number //= base\n    \n    # The remainders give the digits of the number in reverse order\n    digits.reverse()\n    return \'\'.join(map(str, digits))\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_n_representation = decimal_to_base_n(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_n_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base \\(5\\) representation of the decimal number \\(555_{10}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\).', 'To convert a decimal number to another base, we repeatedly divide the number by the new base and keep track of the remainders. The conversion of $555_{10}$ to base $5$ can be done as follows:\n\n1. Divide 555 by 5, record the remainder.\n2. Divide the quotient from step 1 by 5, record the remainder.\n3. Repeat step 2 until the quotient is 0.\n4. The base-5 representation is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.\n\nLet\'s perform these steps using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n, base):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\n        n //= base\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_representation = decimal_to_base(decimal_num