verrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$, the cross product is:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-2) \\\\ 3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1 \\\\ 1 \\cdot (-2) - 2 \\cdot (-3) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 + 6 \\\\ -9 - 1 \\\\ -2 + 6 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of this vector is:\n\\[\n\\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\sqrt{8^2 + (-10)^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 100 + 16} = \\sqrt{180} = 6\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThe area of triangle $OAB$ is half of this value:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 6\\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nSo the area of triangle $OAB$ is $\\boxed{3\\sqrt{5}}$.', "To find the area of triangle \\(OAB\\), we can use the cross product of vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\). The magnitude of the cross product of two vectors gives the area of the parallelogram formed by those vectors, and the area of the triangle is half of that.\n\nThe cross product of two vectors \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} u_1 \\\\ u_2 \\\\ u_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\\\ v_2 \\\\ v_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} u_2 v_3 - u_3 v_2 \\\\ u_3 v_1 - u_1 v_3 \\\\ u_1 v_2 - u_2 v_1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nThe magnitude of the cross product is:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\| = \\sqrt{(u_2 v_3 - u_3 v_2)^2 + (u_3 v_1 - u_1 v_3)^2 + (u_1 v_2 - u_2 v_1)^2}\n\\]\nFor our vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\), the cross product is:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-2) \\\\ 3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1 \\\\ 1 \\cdot (-2) - 2 \\cdot (-3) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 + 6 \\\\ -9 - 1 \\\\ -2 + 6 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nThe magnitude of this cross product is:\n\\[\n\\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\sqrt{8^2 + (-10)^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 100 + 16} = \\sqrt{180} = 6\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nThe area of triangle \\(OAB\\) is half of this magnitude:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 6\\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the vectors OA and OB\nOA = np.array([1, 2, 3])\nOB = np.array([-3, -2, 1])\n\n# Compute the cross product of OA and OB\ncross_product = np.cross(OA, OB)\n\n# Compute the magnitude of the cross product\nmagnitude = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\n\n# The area of the triangle is half the magnitude of the cross product\narea = 0.5 * magnitude\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n6.708203932499369\n```\nThe area of triangle \\(OAB\\) is \\(3\\sqrt{5}\\), which is approximately 6.708. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]", "To find the area of the triangle \\(OAB\\), we can use the fact that the area of a triangle formed by vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\) is half the magnitude of the cross product of these vectors. The cross product \\(\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{vmatrix}\n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n1 & 2 & 3 \\\\\n-3 & -2 & 1\n\\end{vmatrix}\n= \\mathbf{i}(2 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-2)) - \\mathbf{j}(1 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-3)) + \\mathbf{k}(1 \\cdot (-2) - 2 \\cdot (-3))\n= \\mathbf{i}(2 + 6) - \\mathbf{j}(1 + 9) + \\mathbf{k}(-2 + 6)\n= 8\\mathbf{i} - 10\\mathbf{j} + 4\\mathbf{k}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of the cross product is:\n\n\\[\n\\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\