in{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we can compute the cross product:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-2) \\\\ 3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1 \\\\ 1 \\cdot (-2) - 2 \\cdot (-3) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 + 6 \\\\ -9 - 1 \\\\ -2 + 6 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nThe magnitude of this vector is:\n\\[\n\\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\sqrt{8^2 + (-10)^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 100 + 16} = \\sqrt{180} = 6\\sqrt{5}.\n\\]\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 6\\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}.\n\\]\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the vectors OA and OB\nOA = np.array([1, 2, 3])\nOB = np.array([-3, -2, 1])\n\n# Compute the cross product of OA and OB\ncross_product = np.cross(OA, OB)\n\n# Compute the magnitude of the cross product\nmagnitude = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\n\n# The area of the triangle is half the magnitude of the cross product\narea = 0.5 * magnitude\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n6.708203932499369\n```\nThe computed area of the triangle \\(OAB\\) is \\(3\\sqrt{5}\\), which is approximately \\(6.708\\). Therefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]", "To find the area of triangle $OAB$, we can use the fact that the area of a triangle formed by vectors $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}$ is half the magnitude of the cross product of these vectors. The cross product of two vectors $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}$ in 3D space is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1 \\end{vmatrix}\n= \\mathbf{i}(2 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-2)) - \\mathbf{j}(1 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-3)) + \\mathbf{k}(1 \\cdo