oor|!} + \\binom{22 + 735235|\\lfloor x \\rfloor|}{2356} + \\phi(|\\lfloor x \\rfloor| + 1) + 72x^4 + 3x^3 - 6x^2 + 2x + 1\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   g(x) = e^{3x^2 - |\\lfloor x \\rfloor|!} + \\binom{22 + 735235|\\lfloor x \\rfloor|}{2356} + \\phi(|\\lfloor x \\rfloor| + 1) + 72x^4 + 4x^3 - 11x^2 - 6x + 13\n   \\]\n\n2. **Set $f(x) = g(x)$ and simplify:**\n   \\[\n   e^{3x^2 - |\\lfloor x \\rfloor|!} + \\binom{22 + 735235|\\lfloor x \\rfloor|}{2356} + \\phi(|\\lfloor x \\rfloor| + 1) + 72x^4 + 3x^3 - 6x^2 + 2x + 1 = e^{3x^2 - |\\lfloor x \\rfloor|!} + \\binom{22 + 735235|\\lfloor x \\rfloor|}{2356} + \\phi(|\\lfloor x \\rfloor| + 1) + 72x^4 + 4x^3 - 11x^2 - 6x + 13\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the equation, we get:\n   \\[\n   3x^3 - 6x^2 + 2x + 1 = 4x^3 - 11x^2 - 6x + 13\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   0 = x^3 - 5x^2 - 8x + 12\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve the polynomial equation $x^3 - 5x^2 - 8x + 12 = 0$:**\n   We can use Python to find the roots of this polynomial equation.\n\nLet's implement this in Python using the `numpy` library to find the roots of the polynomial equation.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the coefficients of the polynomial x^3 - 5x^2 - 8x + 12\ncoefficients = [1, -5, -8, 12]\n\n# Find the roots of the polynomial\nroots = np.roots(coefficients)\nprint(roots)\n```\n```output\n[ 6. -2.  1.]\n```\nThe roots of the polynomial equation $x^3 - 5x^2 - 8x + 12 = 0$ are $6$, $-2$, and $1$. Since we are looking for the largest $x$-value at which the graphs of $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ intersect, the largest root is $6$.\n\nTherefore, the largest $x$-value at which the graphs of $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ intersect is $\\boxed{6}$.", "To find the largest $x$-value at which the graphs of the given functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ intersect, we need to solve the equation $f(x) = g(x)$. Let's start by setting up the equation:\n\n\\[ f(x) = g(x) \\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[ e^{3x^2 - |\\lfloor x \\rfloor|!} + \\binom{22 + 735235|\\lfloor x \\rfloor|}{2356} + \\phi(|\\lfloor x \\rfloor| + 1) + 