hbf{a}_2, \\mathbf{a}_3$ to find $\\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} -13 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$.\n\nLet's implement this in Python using sympy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the symbols for the components of a1, a2, a3\na11, a12, a13 = sp.symbols('a11 a12 a13')\na21, a22, a23 = sp.symbols('a21 a22 a23')\na31, a32, a33 = sp.symbols('a31 a32 a33')\n\n# Define the equations based on the given conditions\neq1 = sp.Eq(3*a11 + a21, 2)\neq2 = sp.Eq(3*a12 + a22, 4)\neq3 = sp.Eq(3*a13 + a23, -3)\neq4 = sp.Eq(-5*a11 + 2*a21 + 2*a31, 0)\neq5 = sp.Eq(-5*a12 + 2*a22 + 2*a32, -5)\neq6 = sp.Eq(-5*a13 + 2*a23 + 2*a33, -5)\n\n# Solve the system of equations\nsolution = sp.solve((eq1, eq2, eq3, eq4, eq5, eq6), (a11, a12, a13, a21, a22, a23, a31, a32, a33))\n\n# Extract the values of a1, a2, a3\na1 = sp.Matrix([solution[a11], solution[a12], solution[a13]])\na2 = sp.Matrix([solution[a21], solution[a22], solution[a23]])\na3 = sp.Matrix([solution[a31], solution[a32], solution[a33]])\n\n# Define the vector we need to find the image of\nv = sp.Matrix([-13, 3, 4])\n\n# Compute A * v\nAv = -13*a1 + 3*a2 + 4*a3\nprint(Av)\n```\n```output\nKeyError: a33\n```\nIt seems that the solution did not provide values for all the components of the matrix $\\mathbf{A}$. This indicates that we need to re-evaluate our approach to solving the system of equations. Let's solve the system step-by-step manually and then use the results to find the desired vector.\n\nFrom the first equation:\n\\[\n3\\mathbf{a}_1 + \\mathbf{a}_2 = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nWe can express $\\mathbf{a}_2$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a}_1$:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a}_2 = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} - 3\\mathbf{a}_1\n\\]\n\nSubstitute $\\mathbf{a}_2$ into the second equation:\n\\[\n-5\\mathbf{a}_1 + 2\\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} - 3\\mathbf{a}_1\\right) + 2\\mathbf{a}_3 = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[\n-