e solve the equation for \\(x\\) to express \\(t\\) in terms of \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = 8 + 2t \\implies 2t = x - 8 \\implies t = \\frac{x - 8}{2}.\n\\]\nNow substitute this expression for \\(t\\) into the equation for \\(y\\):\n\\[\ny = -1 + 3\\left(\\frac{x - 8}{2}\\right).\n\\]\nSimplify the right-hand side:\n\\[\ny = -1 + \\frac{3x - 24}{2} = -1 + \\frac{3x}{2} - 12 = \\frac{3x}{2} - 13.\n\\]\nSo the equation of the line is:\n\\[\ny = \\frac{3}{2}x - 13.\n\\]\nThus, the ordered pair \\((m, b)\\) is \\(\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -13\\right)\\).\n\nLet's verify this using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the parameterized equations\r\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define symbols\r\nt, x, y = symbols('t x y')\r\n\r\n# Parameterized equations\r\nx_eq = Eq(x, 8 + 2*t)\r\ny_eq = Eq(y, -1 + 3*t)\r\n\r\n# Solve for t in terms of x\r\nt_expr = solve(x_eq, t)[0]\r\n\r\n# Substitute t into the y equation\r\ny_expr = y_eq.subs(t, t_expr)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression to get y in terms of x\r\ny_simplified = y_expr.simplify()\r\n\r\n# Extract the slope (m) and y-intercept (b)\r\nm = y_simplified.rhs.coeff(x)\r\nb = y_simplified.rhs.coeff(x, 0)\r\n\r\nprint(((m, b)))\n```\n```output\n(0, -1)\n```\nIt seems there was an error in the symbolic computation. Let's recheck the steps manually and correct the code if necessary.\n\nThe steps to derive the equation \\(y = mx + b\\) are correct. We should recheck the substitution and simplification process. Let's redo the substitution and simplification manually and then verify it again with Python.\n\nWe have:\n\\[ x = 8 + 2t \\implies t = \\frac{x - 8}{2}. \\]\nSubstituting \\( t \\) into the equation for \\( y \\):\n\\[ y = -1 + 3\\left(\\frac{x - 8}{2}\\right) = -1 + \\frac{3x - 24}{2} = -1 + \\frac{3x}{2} - 12 = \\frac{3x}{2} - 13. \\]\n\nSo, the equation is \\( y = \\frac{3}{2}x - 13 \\), and the ordered pair \\((m, b)\\) is \\(\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -13\\right)\\).\n\nLet's correct the Python code to ens