o ensure the accuracy of our result.\n```python\n# Given data\narea_ABC = 6  # area of triangle ABC in square centimeters\nratio_sides = 1 / 5  # ratio of the sides BC to CD\n\n# The ratio of the areas of similar triangles is the square of the ratio of their corresponding sides\nratio_areas = ratio_sides ** 2\n\n# Calculate the area of triangle CDE\narea_CDE = area_ABC / ratio_areas\nprint(area_CDE)\n```\n```output\n150.0\n```\nThe area of \\(\\triangle CDE\\) is \\(\\boxed{150}\\) square centimeters.", "To solve the problem, let's break it down step-by-step:\n\n1. **Understand the Problem:**\n   - We have a triangle \\( \\triangle ABC \\) with an area of 6 square centimeters.\n   - \\( \\overline{AB} \\parallel \\overline{DE} \\).\n   - \\( BD = 4BC \\).\n\n2. **Determine the Relationship Between the Triangles:**\n   - Since \\( \\overline{AB} \\parallel \\overline{DE} \\), triangles \\( \\triangle ABC \\) and \\( \\triangle CDE \\) are similar.\n   - The ratio of the corresponding sides of similar triangles is the same. Since \\( BD = 4BC \\), the total length \\( CD = BC + BD = BC + 4BC = 5BC \\). Therefore, the ratio of the sides \\( CD:BC = 5:1 \\).\n\n3. **Area Ratio of Similar Triangles:**\n   - The ratio of the areas of similar triangles is the square of the ratio of their corresponding sides. So, the ratio of the areas of \\( \\triangle CDE \\) to \\( \\triangle ABC \\) is \\( (5/1)^2 = 25 \\).\n\n4. **Calculate the Area of \\( \\triangle CDE \\):**\n   - Since the area of \\( \\triangle ABC \\) is 6 square centimeters, the area of \\( \\triangle CDE \\) is \\( 25 \\times 6 = 150 \\) square centimeters.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python and sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Given area of triangle ABC\narea_ABC = 6\n\n# Ratio of the sides CD:BC = 5:1\nratio = 5\n\n# The ratio of the areas of similar triangles is the square of the ratio of their corresponding sides\narea_ratio = ratio**2\n\n# Calculate the area of triangle CDE\narea_CDE = area_ratio * area_ABC\n\nprint(area_CDE)\n```\n```output\n150\n```\nThe area of \\(\\triangle CDE\\) is \\(\\boxed{150}\\) square centimeters.", "To solve the problem, we need to use the properties of similar triangles and the given relationships between the segments.\n\nGiven:\n1. The area of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is 6 square centimeters.\n2. \\(\\overline{AB} \\parallel \\overline{DE}\\).\n3. \\(BD = 4BC\\).\n\nSince \\(\\overline{AB} \\parallel \\overline{DE}\\), \\(\\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle CDE\\) (by AA similarity). The ratio of the corresponding sides of the triangles will be the same.\n\nLet's denote the length of \\(BC\\) as \\(x\\). Then \\(BD = 4x\\), and \\(CD = BC + BD = x + 4x = 5x\\). The ratio of the corresponding sides of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) and \\(\\triangle CDE\\) is \\(BC : CD = x : 5x = 1 : 5\\).\n\nThe ratio of the areas of two similar triangles is the square of the ratio of their corresponding sides. So, the ratio of the areas of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) and \\(\\triangle CDE\\) is \\((1/5)^2 = 1/25\\).\n\nGiven that the area of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is 6 square centimeters, we can set up the following equation to find the area of \\(\\triangle CDE\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\text{Area of } \\triangle ABC}{\\text{Area of } \\triangle CDE} = \\frac{1}{25}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{6}{\\text{Area of } \\triangle CDE} = \\frac{1}{25}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area of } \\triangle CDE = 6 \\times 25 = 150 \\text{ square centimeters}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given area of triangle ABC\narea_ABC = 6\n\n# The ratio of the corresponding sides of the triangles is 1:5\n# The ratio of the areas of the triangles is (1/5)^2 = 1/25\nratio_of_areas = 1 / 25\n\n# Calculate the area of triangle CDE\narea_CDE = area_ABC / ratio_of_areas\nprint(area_CDE)\n```\n```output\n150.0\n```\nThe area of \\(\\triangle CDE\\) is \\(\\boxed{150}\\) square centimeters.", "To solve this problem, we need to use the properties of similar triangles and the given area of \\