implies 2A + B = 14\n\\]\n\nNow we have two equations with two variables:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n2A + B = 14 \\\\\n5B = 3A - 8\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nWe can solve these equations step by step. First, we solve the second equation for \\(B\\):\n\\[\nB = \\frac{3A - 8}{5}\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute this expression for \\(B\\) into the first equation:\n\\[\n2A + \\frac{3A - 8}{5} = 14\n\\]\n\nMultiply through by 5 to clear the fraction:\n\\[\n10A + 3A - 8 = 70 \\implies 13A - 8 = 70 \\implies 13A = 78 \\implies A = 6\n\\]\n\nNow we can find \\(B\\) using \\(B = \\frac{3A - 8}{5}\\):\n\\[\nB = \\frac{3(6) - 8}{5} = \\frac{18 - 8}{5} = \\frac{10}{5} = 2\n\\]\n\nFinally, we can find \\(C\\) using \\(C = A + 4\\):\n\\[\nC = 6 + 4 = 10\n\\]\n\nSo Chris's current age is \\(10\\). Let's verify this solution using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the ages\nA = 6\nB = 2\nC = 10\n\n# Verify the conditions\naverage_age = (A + B + C) / 3\nfour_years_ago_chris = C - 4\nben_age_in_four_years = B + 4\namy_age_in_four_years = A + 4\n\n# Check the conditions\ncondition1 = average_age == 6\ncondition2 = four_years_ago_chris == A\ncondition3 = ben_age_in_four_years == (3/5) * amy_age_in_four_years\n\nprint(((condition1, condition2, condition3, C)))\n```\n```output\n(True, True, True, 10)\n```\nThe conditions are all satisfied, confirming that the solution is correct. Therefore, Chris's current age is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).", "Let's denote the current ages of Amy, Ben, and Chris as \\(A\\), \\(B\\), and \\(C\\) respectively. According to the problem, the average of their ages is 6, so we can write the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{A + B + C}{3} = 6 \\implies A + B + C = 18\n\\]\n\nFour years ago, Chris was the same age as Amy is now, so we can write:\n\n\\[\nC - 4 = A \\implies C = A + 4\n\\]\n\nIn four years, Ben's age will be \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\) of Amy's age at that time, so we can write:\n\n\\[\nB + 4 = \\frac{3}{5}(A + 4)\n\\]\n\nNow we have three equations:\n1. \\(A + B + C = 18\\