ty of the Circle:**\n   - Since $AB$ is the diameter of the circle, the angle subtended by the diameter in the circle is a right angle (90 degrees). This means $\\angle ACB = 90^\\circ$.\n\n3. **Sum of Angles in a Triangle:**\n   - The sum of the angles in any triangle is $180^\\circ$. So, for $\\triangle ABC$, we have:\n     \\[\n     \\angle A + \\angle B + \\angle ACB = 180^\\circ\n     \\]\n   - Substituting the known values:\n     \\[\n     14^\\circ + \\angle B + 90^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n     \\]\n   - Solving for $\\angle B$:\n     \\[\n     \\angle B = 180^\\circ - 14^\\circ - 90^\\circ = 76^\\circ\n     \\]\n\nSo, the measure of $\\angle B$ is $76^\\circ$. Let's confirm this with Python and sympy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the known angles\nangle_A = 14\nangle_ACB = 90\n\n# Calculate the unknown angle B\nangle_B = 180 - angle_A - angle_ACB\n\nprint(angle_B)\n```\n```output\n76\n```\nThe measure of $\\angle B$ is \\(\\boxed{76}\\) degrees.", "To solve the equation \\(10^x - 10 = 9990\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Add 10 to both sides of the equation to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n\\[10^x = 10000\\]\n\n2. Recognize that 10000 is a power of 10. Specifically, \\(10000 = 10^4\\). So we can rewrite the equation as:\n\\[10^x = 10^4\\]\n\n3. Since the bases are the same, we can set the exponents equal to each other:\n\\[x = 4\\]\n\nWe can verify this solution by substituting \\(x = 4\\) back into the original equation to ensure it holds true. Let's do this using Python to confirm our result.\n```python\n# Define the value of x\nx = 4\n\n# Calculate the left side of the original equation\nleft_side = 10**x - 10\n\n# Check if the left side equals the right side (9990)\nprint(left_side == 9990)\n```\n```output\nTrue\n```\nThe calculation confirms that when \\(x = 4\\), the left side of the equation \\(10^x - 10\\) equals 9990, which matches the right side of the equation. Therefore, the solution is correct.\n\nThe value of \\(x\\) is \\(\\