\\( H \\) lies on the line \\( EG \\), its y-coordinate is 3. So, we solve for \\( t \\):\n     \\[\n     3 = \\frac{x}{3}(t - 3) \\implies 9 = x(t - 3) \\implies t = \\frac{9}{x} + 3\n     \\]\n   - The x-coordinate of \\( H \\) is \\( t = \\frac{9}{x} + 3 \\). Since \\( H \\) lies on the line \\( EG \\), its y-coordinate is 3. Therefore, the coordinates of \\( H \\) are \\( \\left( \\frac{9}{x} + 3, 3 \\right) \\).\n\n6. **Determine the Length \\( BH \\):**\n   - The length \\( BH \\) is the distance between points \\( B = (3, 0) \\) and \\( H = \\left( \\frac{9}{x} + 3, 3 \\right) \\). Using the distance formula:\n     \\[\n     BH = \\sqrt{\\left( \\frac{9}{x} + 3 - 3 \\right)^2 + (3 - 0)^2} = \\sqrt{\\left( \\frac{9}{x} \\right)^2 + 3^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{81}{x^2} + 9}\n     \\]\n   - Since \\( BH = x \\), we have:\n     \\[\n     x = \\sqrt{\\frac{81}{x^2} + 9}\n     \\]\n   - Squaring both sides, we get:\n     \\[\n     x^2 = \\frac{81}{x^2} + 9 \\implies x^4 = 81 + 9x^2 \\implies x^4 - 9x^2 - 81 = 0\n     \\]\n   - Let \\( y = x^2 \\). Then the equation becomes:\n     \\[\n     y^2 - 9y - 81 = 0\n     \\]\n   - Solving this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( y = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\):\n     \\[\n     y = \\frac{9 \\pm \\sqrt{81 + 324}}{2} = \\frac{9 \\pm \\sqrt{405}}{2} = \\frac{9 \\pm 9\\sqrt{5}}{2}\n     \\]\n   - Since \\( y = x^2 \\) must be positive, we take the positive root:\n     \\[\n     y = \\frac{9 + 9\\sqrt{5}}{2} \\implies x^2 = \\frac{9 + 9\\sqrt{5}}{2} \\implies x = \\sqrt{\\frac{9 + 9\\sqrt{5}}{2}}\n     \\]\n   - Simplifying further, we get:\n     \\[\n     x = \\frac{3\\sqrt{2 + 2\\sqrt{5}}}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{2 + 2\\sqrt{5}} \\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{2} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{4 + 4\\sqrt{5}}}{2} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{2(2 + 2\\sqrt{5})}}{2} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{2 + 2\\sqrt{5}}}{2} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{2(1 + \\sqrt{5})}}{2} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{1 + \\sqrt{5}}}{2