 and tangents. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Understand the Geometry:**\n   - Since $HO$ and $HN$ are tangent to the circle at $O$ and $N$ respectively, the angles $\\angle HOJ$ and $\\angle HNJ$ are right angles (90 degrees) because the radius of a circle is perpendicular to the tangent at the point of tangency.\n   - The quadrilateral $HONJ$ is formed by the tangent lines and the radii of the circle. Since $HO$ and $HN$ are tangents and $O$ and $N$ are points of tangency, the line segments $HO$ and $HN$ are equal in length.\n   - The angle $\\angle J$ is the central angle subtended by the arc $ON$.\n\n2. **Calculate the Angles:**\n   - The angle $\\angle H$ is the angle formed by the tangents $HO$ and $HN$. Since $HO$ and $HN$ are tangents and form right angles with the radii $JO$ and $JN$ respectively, the angle $\\angle H$ is the external angle to the triangle $HOJ$ and $HNJ$.\n   - The sum of the angles in quadrilateral $HONJ$ is 360 degrees. Since $\\angle HOJ$ and $\\angle HNJ$ are each 90 degrees, the sum of $\\angle J$ and $\\angle H$ must be 180 degrees.\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\n   - The sum of $\\angle J$ and $\\angle H$ is 180 degrees.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python and sympy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the angles\nangle_HOJ = 90  # Angle formed by tangent HO and radius JO\nangle_HNJ = 90  # Angle formed by tangent HN and radius JN\n\n# The sum of the angles in quadrilateral HONJ is 360 degrees\n# So, angle J + angle H + angle HOJ + angle HNJ = 360\n# angle J + angle H + 90 + 90 = 360\n# angle J + angle H = 360 - 180 = 180\n\nangle_J_plus_angle_H = 360 - (angle_HOJ + angle_HNJ)\nprint(angle_J_plus_angle_H)\n```\n```output\n180\n```\nThe sum of the measures of $\\angle J$ and $\\angle H$ is \\(\\boxed{180}\\) degrees.", 'In circle $J$, $HO$ and $HN$ are tangent to the circle at $O$ and $N$. Find the number of degrees in the sum of $m\\angle J$ and $m\\angle H$. [asy]\nsize(150);\nimport graph;\npair J = (0,0), H = (6,0), O, N;\npath circ 