(4 \\dfrac{5}{8}\\right)^{55} \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{8}{37}\\right)^{55} = \\left(4 \\dfrac{5}{8} \\cdot \\dfrac{8}{37}\\right)^{55}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to convert the mixed number \\(4 \\dfrac{5}{8}\\) to an improper fraction:\n\n\\[\n4 \\dfrac{5}{8} = \\dfrac{4 \\cdot 8 + 5}{8} = \\dfrac{37}{8}\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute this back into the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\dfrac{37}{8} \\cdot \\dfrac{8}{37}\\right)^{55} = \\left(\\dfrac{37 \\cdot 8}{8 \\cdot 37}\\right)^{55} = \\left(\\dfrac{296}{296}\\right)^{55} = 1^{55} = 1\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the values\nmixed_fraction = 37 / 8\nfraction = 8 / 37\nexponent = 55\n\n# Calculate the expression\nresult = (mixed_fraction * fraction) ** exponent\nprint(result)\n```", "To solve the expression \\(\\left(4\\dfrac{5}{8}\\right)^{55} \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{8}{37}\\right)^{55}\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the mixed number \\(4\\dfrac{5}{8}\\) to an improper fraction.\n2. Simplify the expression by using the properties of exponents.\n\nFirst, let's convert \\(4\\dfrac{5}{8}\\) to an improper fraction:\n\\[4\\dfrac{5}{8} = 4 + \\dfrac{5}{8} = \\dfrac{32}{8} + \\dfrac{5}{8} = \\dfrac{37}{8}.\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\\[\\left(\\dfrac{37}{8}\\right)^{55} \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{8}{37}\\right)^{55}.\\]\n\nUsing the property of exponents \\((a/b)^n \\cdot (b/a)^n = (a/b \\cdot b/a)^n = 1^n = 1\\), we can simplify the expression:\n\\[\\left(\\dfrac{37}{8}\\right)^{55} \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{8}{37}\\right)^{55} = \\left(\\dfrac{37}{8} \\cdot \\dfrac{8}{37}\\right)^{55} = 1^{55} = 1.\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the fractions and the exponent\nfraction1 = (37, 8)\nfraction2 = (8, 37)\nexponent = 55\n\n# Calculate the expression\nresult = (fraction1[0] / fraction1[1]) ** exponent * (fraction2[0] 