e value of \\( c \\) is 64.\n\nNext, consider the case where \\( p = 2 \\). Then:\n\\[\na = 2 + q + r,\n\\]\n\\[\na^2 = 2(2q + qr + 2r) + 81 = 2(2q + qr + 2r) + 81.\n\\]\nSubstituting \\( a = 2 + q + r \\) into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n(2 + q + r)^2 = 2(2q + qr + 2r) + 81.\n\\]\nExpanding and simplifying, we have:\n\\[\n4 + 4q + 4r + q^2 + 2qr + r^2 = 4q + 2qr + 4r + 81,\n\\]\n\\[\n4 + q^2 + r^2 = 81,\n\\]\n\\[\nq^2 + r^2 = 77.\n\\]\nWe need to find pairs of positive integers \\( (q, r) \\) that satisfy this equation. The possible pairs are \\( (5, 8) \\) and \\( (8, 5) \\). For \\( q = 5 \\) and \\( r = 8 \\), we have:\n\\[\na = 2 + 5 + 8 = 15.\n\\]\nNow, we calculate \\( c \\):\n\\[\npqr = 2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 8 = 80,\n\\]\n\\[\nc = 2 \\cdot 80 = 160.\n\\]\nFor \\( q = 8 \\) and \\( r = 5 \\), we get the same value for \\( a \\) and \\( c \\). So, another possible value of \\( c \\) is 160.\n\nSince Jon says there are still two possible values of \\( c \\) after Steve gives him \\( a = 13 \\), the two possible values of \\( c \\) are 64 and 160. The sum of these values is:\n\\[\n64 + 160 = 224.\n\\]\nThus, the sum of the two possible values of \\( c \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{224}.\n\\]", "To solve the problem, we need to analyze the polynomial $P(x) = 2x^3 - 2ax^2 + (a^2 - 81)x - c$ with roots that are all positive integers. Let's denote the roots by $r_1, r_2,$ and $r_3$. Using Vieta's formulas, we can relate the coefficients of the polynomial to its roots:\n\n1. $r_1 + r_2 + r_3 = a$\n2. $r_1r_2 + r_2r_3 + r_3r_1 = \\frac{a^2 - 81}{2}$\n3. $r_1r_2r_3 = \\frac{c}{2}$\n\nFrom the first equation, we have $a = r_1 + r_2 + r_3$. Substituting $a$ into the second equation, we get:\n\n\\[ r_1r_2 + r_2r_3 + r_3r_1 = \\frac{(r_1 + r_2 + r_3)^2 - 81}{2} \\]\n\nExpanding the right-hand side, we get:\n\n\\[ r_1r_2 + r_2r_3 + r_3r_1 = \\frac{r_1^2 + r_2^2 + r_3^2 + 2(r_1r_2 + r_2r_3 + r_3r_1) - 81}{2} \\]\n\nMultiplying through by 2, we obtain:\n\n\\[ 2(r_1r_2 + r_2r_3 + r_3r_1) 