od of 10. To confirm this, let's compute a few more terms:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nx_{13} &= x_{12} - x_{11} + x_{10} - x_9 = 375 - 211 + (-267) - (-523) = 420, \\\\\nx_{14} &= x_{13} - x_{12} + x_{11} - x_{10} = 420 - 375 + 211 - (-267) = 523, \\\\\nx_{15} &= x_{14} - x_{13} + x_{12} - x_{11} = 523 - 420 + 375 - 211 = 267, \\\\\nx_{16} &= x_{15} - x_{14} + x_{13} - x_{12} = 267 - 523 + 420 - 375 = -211, \\\\\nx_{17} &= x_{16} - x_{15} + x_{14} - x_{13} = -211 - 267 + 523 - 420 = -375, \\\\\nx_{18} &= x_{17} - x_{16} + x_{15} - x_{14} = -375 - (-211) + 267 - 523 = -420, \\\\\nx_{19} &= x_{18} - x_{17} + x_{16} - x_{15} = -420 - (-375) + (-211) - 267 = -523, \\\\\nx_{20} &= x_{19} - x_{18} + x_{17} - x_{16} = -523 - (-420) + (-375) - (-211) = -267, \\\\\nx_{21} &= x_{20} - x_{19} + x_{18} - x_{17} = -267 - (-523) + (-420) - (-375) = 211, \\\\\nx_{22} &= x_{21} - x_{20} + x_{19} - x_{18} = 211 - (-267) + (-523) - (-420) = 375.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nWe can see that the sequence repeats every 10 terms. Therefore, we can find \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\) by determining their positions within the first 10 terms:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nx_{531} &= x_{531 \\mod 10} = x_1 = 211, \\\\\nx_{753} &= x_{753 \\mod 10} = x_3 = 420, \\\\\nx_{975} &= x_{975 \\mod 10} = x_5 = 267.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we sum these values:\n\n\\[\nx_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975} = 211 + 420 + 267 = 898.\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the initial terms of the sequence\nx = [211, 375, 420, 523]\n\n# Generate the sequence up to the first 10 terms to confirm the periodicity\nfor n in range(4, 10):\n    x.append(x[n-1] - x[n-2] + x[n-3] - x[n-4])\n\n# The sequence is periodic with a period of 10\nperiod = 10\n\n# Find the values of x_531, x_753, and x_975\nx_531 = x[531 % period - 1]\nx_753 = x[753 % period - 1]\nx_975 = x[975 % period - 1]\n\n# Sum the values\nresult = x_531 + x_753 + x_975\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n89