mbols('p')\r\n\r\n# Define the inequalities\r\nineq1 = 54*p - 144 <= 0\r\nineq2 = 12 - 20*p < 0\r\n\r\n# Solve the inequalities\r\nsol1 = solve(ineq1, p)\r\nsol2 = solve(ineq2, p)\r\n\r\n# Find the intersection of the solutions\r\nsolution = S.Intersection(sol1, sol2)\r\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\nAttributeError: Attribute 'Intersection' was not installed on SymPy registry S\n```\nIt seems there was an error with the use of `S.Intersection`. Instead, we can use `sympy.solve_univariate_inequality` to solve the inequalities and then find the intersection manually. Let's correct the code and find the solution again.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, solve_univariate_inequality\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\np = symbols('p')\r\n\r\n# Define the inequalities\r\nineq1 = 54*p - 144 <= 0\r\nineq2 = 12 - 20*p < 0\r\n\r\n# Solve the inequalities\r\nsol1 = solve_univariate_inequality(ineq1, p, relational=False)\r\nsol2 = solve_univariate_inequality(ineq2, p, relational=False)\r\n\r\n# Find the intersection of the solutions\r\nsolution = sol1.intersect(sol2)\r\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\nInterval.Lopen(3/5, 8/3)\n```\nThe solution to the system of inequalities \\( 0 \\ge 54p - 144 \\) and \\( 0 > 12 - 20p \\) is the interval \\(\\left( \\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{8}{3} \\right]\\).\n\nTherefore, the final answer in interval notation is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left( \\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{8}{3} \\right]}\n\\]", "To solve the problem, we need to find the values of \\( p \\) that satisfy both inequalities \\( 0 \\ge 54p - 144 \\) and \\( 0 > 12 - 20p \\). Let's break this down step by step.\n\n1. Solve the first inequality \\( 0 \\ge 54p - 144 \\):\n\\[ 0 \\ge 54p - 144 \\]\n\\[ 144 \\ge 54p \\]\n\\[ \\frac{144}{54} \\ge p \\]\n\\[ \\frac{8}{3} \\ge p \\]\n\\[ p \\le \\frac{8}{3} \\]\n\n2. Solve the second inequality \\( 0 > 12 - 20p \\):\n\\[ 0 > 12 - 20p \\]\n\\[ 20p > 12 \\]\n\\[ p > \\frac{12}{20} \\]\n\\[ p > \\frac{3}{5} \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the intersection of the 