mbinations:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{14}{5}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to subtract the number of ways to form a subcommittee that consists entirely of Republicans or entirely of Democrats. The number of ways to choose 5 Republicans from 8 is:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{8}{5}\n\\]\n\nAnd the number of ways to choose 5 Democrats from 6 is:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{6}{5}\n\\]\n\nSo, the number of ways to form a subcommittee with at least one member from each party is:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{14}{5} - \\left(\\binom{8}{5} + \\binom{6}{5}\\right)\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python.\n```python\nfrom math import comb\n\n# Total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14\ntotal_ways = comb(14, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose 5 Republicans from 8\nways_all_republicans = comb(8, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose 5 Democrats from 6\nways_all_democrats = comb(6, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to form a subcommittee with at least one member from each party\nways_at_least_one_from_each_party = total_ways - (ways_all_republicans + ways_all_democrats)\nprint(ways_at_least_one_from_each_party)\n```\n```output\n1940\n```\nThe number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, where the subcommittee must include at least one member from each party, is \\(\\boxed{1940}\\).", "To solve the problem of forming a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats with at least one member from each party, we can use the principle of complementary counting. Specifically, we can find the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members and subtract the number of ways to form a subcommittee with only Republicans or only Democrats.\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 14 people.\n2. Calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that are all Republicans.\n3. Calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that are all Democrat