tal_ways - ways_all_republicans - ways_all_democrats\n\nprint(ways_at_least_one_from_each_party)\n```\n```output\n1940\n```\nThe number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, with at least one member from each party, is \\(\\boxed{1940}\\).", "To simplify the given expression \\(\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}+\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}+\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{5}}}\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Simplify each term in the numerator separately.\n2. Combine the simplified terms in the numerator.\n3. Simplify the fraction inside the square root.\n4. Take the square root of the simplified fraction.\n\nLet's break it down step-by-step:\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\dfrac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{5 \\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{4 \\cdot 5} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n   \\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{845} = \\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5} = 13\\sqrt{5}\n   \\]\n   So,\n   \\[\n   \\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n   \\]\n\n3. Simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n   \\]\n\n4. Combine the simplified terms in the numerator:\n   \\[\n   \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5} = \\dfrac{9\\sqrt{5} + 52\\sqrt{5} + 108\\sqrt{5}}{36} = \\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n   \\]\n\n5. Simplify the fraction inside the square root:\n   \\[\n   \\dfrac{\\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36 \\cdot \\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{169}{36}\n   \\]\n\n6. Take the square root of the simplified fraction:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\dfrac{169}{36}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\dfrac{13}{6}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the simplified expression is \\(\\dfrac{13}{6}\\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\r\n\r\n# Define the expression\r\nnumerator = (5 / sp.sqrt(80)) + (sp.sqrt(845) / 9) + sp.sqrt(45)\r\ndenominator = sp.sqrt(5)\r\nexpression = sp.sqrt(numerator / denominator)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = sp.simplify(expression)\r\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```\n```output\n13/6\n```\nThe simplified expression is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{13}{6}}\\).", "To solve the given expression, we need to simplify the numerator and the denominator separately, and then combine them to get the final simplified fraction.\n\nThe expression is:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} + \\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} + \\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\nLet's break it down step by step:\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\frac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{5 \\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{4 \\cdot 5} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n\\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{845} = \\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5} = 13\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n\\]\n\n3. Simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nNow, combine these simplified terms in the numerator:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nTo add these fractions, we need a common denominator. The least common multiple of 4, 9, and 1 is 36:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} = \\frac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} = \\frac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad 3\\sqrt{5} = \\frac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\frac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\frac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\frac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36} = \\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n\\]\n\nNow, we can substitute this back into the original expression:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{169}{36}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\frac{13}{6}\n\\]\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{13}{6}}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code for accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\r\n\r\n# Define the components\r\nnumerator_1 = 5 / math.sqrt(80)\r\nnumerator_2 = math.sqrt(845) / 9\r\nnumerator_3 = math.sqrt(45)\r\n\r\n# Combine the numerators\r\nnumerator = numerator_1 + numerator_2 + numerator_3\r\n\r\n# Denominator\r\ndenominator = math.sqrt(5)\r\n\r\n# Final expression\r\nresult = math.sqrt(numerator / denominator)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the result to a fraction\r\nfrom fractions import Fraction\r\nsimplified_result = Fraction(result).limit_denominator()\r\n\r\nprint(simplified_result)\n```", "Let's break down the expression step by step and simplify it using Python and SymPy.\n\nThe given expression is:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} + \\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} + \\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we will simplify the terms inside the square root:\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\frac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{5 \\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{4 \\cdot 5} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n\\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{845} = \\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5} = \\sqrt{169} \\cdot \\sqrt{5} = 13\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n\\]\n\n3. Simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = \\sqrt{9} \\cdot \\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nNow, we can substitute these simplified terms back into the expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we will combine the terms in the numerator:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5} = \\sqrt{5} \\left( \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{13}{9} + 3 \\right)\n\\]\n\nTo combine the fractions, we need a common denominator:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{9}{36}, \\quad \\frac{13}{9} = \\frac{52}{36}, \\quad 3 = \\frac{108}{36}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{13}{9} + 3 = \\frac{9}{36} + \\frac{52}{36} + \\frac{108}{36} = \\frac{9 + 52 + 108}{36} = \\frac{169}{36}\n\\]\nTherefore,\n\\[\n\\sqrt{5} \\left( \\frac{169}{36} \\right) = \\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n\\]\n\nNow, we can substitute this back into the original expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{169}{36}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we take the square root of this result:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{169}{36}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\frac{13}{6}\n\\]\n\nSo, the simplified expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{13}{6}}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python and SymPy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the expression\nnumerator = sp.Rational(5, sp.sqrt(80)) + sp.sqrt(845)/9 + sp.sqrt(45)\ndenominator = sp.sqrt(5)\nexpression = sp.sqrt(numerator / denominator)\n\n# Simplify the expression\nsimplified_expression = sp.simplify(expression)\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```", "To solve the problem, let's break it down step by step. We need to simplify the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} + \\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} + \\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\n1. Simplify the individual terms in the numerator:\n   - Simplify \\(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n     \\[\n     \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\frac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{5 \\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{4 \\cdot 5} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n     \\]\n   - Simplify \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n     \\[\n     \\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\frac{\\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5}}{9} = \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n     \\]\n   - Simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n     \\[\n     \\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n     \\]\n2. Combine the simplified terms in the numerator:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5} = \\sqrt{5} \\left( \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{13}{9} + 3 \\right)\n   \\]\n   To add the fractions, find a common denominator:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{9}{36}, \\quad \\frac{13}{9} = \\frac{52}{36}, \\quad 3 = \\frac{108}{36}\n   \\]\n   So,\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{13}{9} + 3 = \\frac{9 + 52 + 108}{36} = \\frac{169}{36}\n   \\]\n   Therefore,\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5} = \\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n   \\]\n3. Substitute this back into the original expression:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36 \\cdot \\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{169}{36}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\frac{13}{6}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the simplified fraction is \\(\\frac{13}{6}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import sqrt, Rational\r\n\r\n# Define the expression\r\nnumerator = Rational(5, sqrt(80)) + Rational(sqrt(845), 9) + sqrt(45)\r\ndenominator = sqrt(5)\r\nexpression = sqrt(numerator / denominator)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = expression.simplify()\r\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```\n```output\nTypeError: invalid input: 5*sqrt(2)\n```\nIt seems there was an error in the way the expression was defined. Let's correct it by using the `sqrt` function from the `sympy` library to handle the square roots properly. We'll redefine the expression step by step to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import sqrt, Rational\r\n\r\n# Define the components of the expression\r\nterm1 = Rational(5) / sqrt(80)\r\nterm2 = sqrt(845) / 9\r\nterm3 = sqrt(45)\r\n\r\n# Combine the terms in the numerator\r\nnumerator = term1 + term2 + term3\r\n\r\n# Define the denominator\r\ndenominator = sqrt(5)\r\n\r\n# Define the full expression\r\nexpression = sqrt(numerator / denominator)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = expression.simplify()\r\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```\n```output\n13/6\n```\nThe simplified expression is indeed \\(\\frac{13}{6}\\).\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{13}{6}}\n\\]", "To simplify the given expression \\(\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}+\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}+\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt5}}\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Simplify each term in the numerator separately.\n2. Combine the simplified terms in the numerator.\n3. Divide the combined numerator by \\(\\sqrt{5}\\).\n4. Take the square root of the resulting fraction.\n\nLet's break it down step-by-step and use Python to ensure accuracy.\n\n### Step 1: Simplify each term in the numerator\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\dfrac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{5\\sqrt{5}}{20} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n   \\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{845} = \\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5} = 13\\sqrt{5}\n   \\]\n   So,\n   \\[\n   \\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n   \\]\n\n3. Simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Combine the simplified terms in the numerator\n\nThe numerator is:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nTo combine these terms, we need a common denominator. The least common multiple of 4, 9, and 1 is 36. So we rewrite each term with the common denominator:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} = \\dfrac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} = \\dfrac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad 3\\sqrt{5} = \\dfrac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n\\]\nAdding these together, we get:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\dfrac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\dfrac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36} = \\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Divide the combined numerator by \\(\\sqrt{5}\\)\n\nThe expression now becomes:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{169}{36}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\dfrac{13}{6}\n\\]\n\nSo the final simplified fraction is \\(\\dfrac{13}{6}\\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import sqrt, Rational\r\n\r\n# Define the expression\r\nnumerator = Rational(5, sqrt(80)) + Rational(sqrt(845), 9) + sqrt(45)\r\ndenominator = sqrt(5)\r\nexpression = sqrt(numerator / denominator)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = expression.simplify()\r\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```\n```output\nTypeError: invalid input: 4*sqrt(5)\n```\nIt seems there was an issue with the way the expression was defined in the code. Let's correct it and simplify the expression step-by-step using SymPy.\n\nHere's the corrected code:\n\n```python\nfrom sympy import sqrt, Rational, simplify\r\n\r\n# Define the terms\r\nterm1 = Rational(5) / sqrt(80)\r\nterm2 = sqrt(845) / 9\r\nterm3 = sqrt(45)\r\n\r\n# Combine the terms in the numerator\r\nnumerator = term1 + term2 + term3\r\n\r\n# Define the denominator\r\ndenominator = sqrt(5)\r\n\r\n# Define the expression\r\nexpression = sqrt(numerator / denominator)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = simplify(expression)\r\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```\n```output\n13/6\n```\nThe simplified expression is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{13}{6}}\\). This confirms our earlier manual calculation.", "To simplify the given expression, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Simplify each term in the numerator separately.\n2. Sum the simplified terms in the numerator.\n3. Divide the sum by \\(\\sqrt{5}\\) and simplify the resulting expression.\n\nLet's break down the expression step-by-step.\n\nThe given expression is:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}+\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}+\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\nFirst, simplify each term in the numerator:\n1. Simplify \\(\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n\\[\n\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\dfrac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{5 \\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{4 \\cdot 5} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n\\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{845} = \\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5} = 13\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n\\]\n\n3. Simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nNow, sum these simplified terms:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nTo add these terms, we need a common denominator. The common denominator for 4, 9, and 1 is 36:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} = \\dfrac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} = \\dfrac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad 3\\sqrt{5} = \\dfrac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\dfrac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\dfrac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\dfrac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36} = \\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n\\]\n\nNow, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{169}{36}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\dfrac{13}{6}\n\\]\n\nSo, the final simplified fraction is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\dfrac{13}{6}}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import sqrt, Rational\r\n\r\n# Define the terms\r\nterm1 = Rational(5, sqrt(80))\r\nterm2 = sqrt(845) / 9\r\nterm3 = sqrt(45)\r\n\r\n# Sum the terms\r\nnumerator = term1 + term2 + term3\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = sqrt(numerator / sqrt(5))\r\n\r\n# Simplify the final result\r\nfinal_result = simplified_expression.simplify()\r\nprint(final_result)\n```", "To solve the given expression, we will break it down step by step and use Python to ensure accuracy.\n\nThe expression we need to simplify is:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}+\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}+\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's simplify the individual components:\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n\\[\n\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\dfrac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{5\\sqrt{5}}{20} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n\\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{845} = \\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5} = 13\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n\\]\n\n3. Simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nNow, we can substitute these simplified forms into the original expression:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine the terms in the numerator:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5} = \\dfrac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\dfrac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\dfrac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36} = \\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36\\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{169}{36}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we take the square root of this fraction:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\dfrac{169}{36}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\dfrac{13}{6}\n\\]\n\nSo the simplified fraction is \\(\\dfrac{13}{6}\\).\n\nLet's verify this using Python to ensure the accuracy of each step.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the expression\nnumerator = sp.Rational(5, sp.sqrt(80)) + sp.sqrt(845)/9 + sp.sqrt(45)\ndenominator = sp.sqrt(5)\nexpression = sp.sqrt(numerator / denominator)\n\n# Simplify the expression\nsimplified_expression = sp.simplify(expression)\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```\n```output\nTypeError: invalid input: 4*sqrt(5)\n```\nIt seems there was an issue with the way the expression was defined in the code. Let's correct the approach and simplify the expression step by step using SymPy.\n\nHere is the corrected code:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the components\nsqrt_80 = sp.sqrt(80)\nsqrt_845 = sp.sqrt(845)\nsqrt_45 = sp.sqrt(45)\nsqrt_5 = sp.sqrt(5)\n\n# Simplify each component\nterm1 = 5 / sqrt_80\nterm2 = sqrt_845 / 9\nterm3 = sqrt_45\n\n# Combine the terms in the numerator\nnumerator = term1 + term2 + term3\n\n# Define the denominator\ndenominator = sqrt_5\n\n# Form the expression\nexpression = sp.sqrt(numerator / denominator)\n\n# Simplify the expression\nsimplified_expression = sp.simplify(expression)\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```\n```output\n13/6\n```\nThe simplified fraction of the given expression is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{13}{6}}\\).", "To simplify th