 we can use the property of binomial coefficients that \\(\\dbinom{n}{k} = \\dbinom{n}{n-k}\\). This property simplifies the calculation because \\(\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\dbinom{31}{3}\\). The binomial coefficient \\(\\dbinom{n}{k}\\) is given by the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nSo, \\(\\dbinom{31}{3}\\) is calculated as:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{3} = \\frac{31!}{3!(31-3)!} = \\frac{31!}{3! \\cdot 28!} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}\n\\]\n\nWe can compute this step by step:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{6} = 31 \\times 5 \\times 29 = 4495\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this calculation using Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the binomial coefficient using the math library\nn = 31\nk = 28\nbinomial_coefficient = math.comb(n, k)\nprint(binomial_coefficient)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe value of \\(\\dbinom{31}{28}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).", "To compute $\\dbinom{31}{28}$, we can use the formula for binomial coefficients, which is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, $n = 31$ and $k = 28$. So we have:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28!(31-28)!} = \\frac{31!}{28!3!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by canceling out the common factorial terms in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29 \\times 28!}{28! \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}\n\\]\n\nNow we can compute the value by evaluating the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{6}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the binomial coefficient using the formula\nn = 31\nk = 28\nbinomial_coefficient = math.comb(n, k)\nprint(binomial_coefficient)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe value of $\\dbinom{31}{28}$ is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).", "To compute $