 + f(1985) \\). Let's calculate the sum:\n\\[ \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} f(n) = \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} \\left( (-2)^{n-1} f(1) + (-2)^{n-1} + (-1)^{n+1} \\left( n - \\frac{1}{3} \\right) \\right) \\]\nWe can split this sum into three parts:\n\\[ \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-2)^{n-1} f(1) \\]\n\\[ \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-2)^{n-1} \\]\n\\[ \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-1)^{n+1} \\left( n - \\frac{1}{3} \\right) \\]\n\nThe first sum is a geometric series:\n\\[ \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-2)^{n-1} f(1) = f(1) \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-2)^{n-1} = f(1) \\frac{1 - (-2)^{1985}}{1 - (-2)} = f(1) \\frac{1 + 2^{1985}}{3} \\]\n\nThe second sum is also a geometric series:\n\\[ \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-2)^{n-1} = \\frac{1 - (-2)^{1985}}{1 - (-2)} = \\frac{1 + 2^{1985}}{3} \\]\n\nThe third sum alternates and can be split into even and odd terms:\n\\[ \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-1)^{n+1} \\left( n - \\frac{1}{3} \\right) = \\sum_{k=1}^{993} \\left( (2k-1) - \\frac{1}{3} \\right) - \\sum_{k=1}^{992} \\left( 2k - \\frac{1}{3} \\right) \\]\n\\[ = \\sum_{k=1}^{993} \\left( 2k - \\frac{4}{3} \\right) - \\sum_{k=1}^{992} \\left( 2k - \\frac{1}{3} \\right) \\]\n\\[ = \\left( 2 \\sum_{k=1}^{993} k - \\frac{4}{3} \\cdot 993 \\right) - \\left( 2 \\sum_{k=1}^{992} k - \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 992 \\right) \\]\n\\[ = \\left( 2 \\cdot \\frac{993 \\cdot 994}{2} - \\frac{4 \\cdot 993}{3} \\right) - \\left( 2 \\cdot \\frac{992 \\cdot 993}{2} - \\frac{992}{3} \\right) \\]\n\\[ = (993 \\cdot 994 - \\frac{4 \\cdot 993}{3}) - (992 \\cdot 993 - \\frac{992}{3}) \\]\n\\[ = 993 \\cdot 994 - 992 \\cdot 993 - \\frac{4 \\cdot 993 - 992}{3} \\]\n\\[ = 993 (994 - 992) - \\frac{4 \\cdot 993 - 992}{3} \\]\n\\[ = 993 \\cdot 2 - \\frac{3972 - 992}{3} \\]\n\\[ = 1986 - \\frac{2980}{3} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{5958 - 2980}{3} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{2978}{3} \\]\n\nCombining all the parts, we get:\n\\[ \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} f(n) = f(1) \\frac{1 + 2^{1985}}{3} + \\frac{1 + 2^{1985}}{3} + \\frac{2978}{3} \\]\nSince \\( f(1) = f(1986) \\), we can use the fact that \\( f(1986) = (-2)^{1985} f(1