 integer solutions to the congruence \\(14u \\equiv 46 \\pmod{100}\\) are \\(47\\) and \\(97\\). The average of these two solutions is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{72}\n\\]", 'The map scale is $3$ inches to $10$ miles. We can set up a proportion to find the distance on the map for $53.25$ miles in real life.\n\\[\n\\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{x \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{159.75}{10} \\text{ inches} = 15.975 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\nTo express this as a fraction, we note that $15.975 = \\frac{15975}{1000}$. Simplifying this fraction:\n\\[\n\\frac{15975}{1000} = \\frac{639}{40}\n\\]\nThus, the distance between the buildings on the map is $\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}$ inches.', "Let's solve the problem step-by-step.\n\n1. **Understand the scale of the map:**\n   - On the map, 3 inches represent 10 miles in real life.\n   - We need to find out how many inches on the map represent 53.25 miles in real life.\n\n2. **Set up the proportion:**\n   - If 3 inches on the map correspond to 10 miles in real life, then \\(x\\) inches on the map would correspond to 53.25 miles in real life.\n   - We can set up the proportion as follows:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{x \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}}\n     \\]\n   - Solving for \\(x\\), we get:\n     \\[\n     x = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the value of \\(x\\):**\n   - Let's calculate this step-by-step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n\n```python\n# Define the given values\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches\nreal_life_distance = 53.25  # miles\nreal_life_distance_per_10_miles = 10  # miles\n\n# Calculate the map distance for 53.25 miles\nmap_distance = (map_distance_per_10_miles * real_life_distance) / real_life_distance_per_10_miles\nprint(map_distance)\n```\n```output\n15.975\n```\nThe calculation shows that the distance between the buildings on the map is \\(15.975\\) inches. To express this as a fraction, we recognize that \\(15.975\\) is the same as \\(15 \\frac{39}{40}\\) or \\(\\frac{639}{40}\\).\n\nSo, the distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\\) inches.", "To determine the distance on the map that corresponds to a real-life distance of 53.25 miles, we can use the given scale of the map. The scale is 3 inches on the map for every 10 miles in real life. We can set up a proportion to solve for the distance on the map.\n\nLet's denote the distance on the map as \\(d\\) inches. The proportion can be set up as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{d \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(d\\):\n\n\\[\nd = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\nd = \\frac{3 \\times 53.25}{10} = \\frac{159.75}{10} = 15.975 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nSince we need the answer as a fraction, we can express 15.975 as a fraction:\n\n\\[\n15.975 = \\frac{15975}{1000} = \\frac{639}{40}\n\\]\n\nThus, the distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\frac{639}{40}\\) inches. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given values\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches\nreal_life_distance = 53.25  # miles\n\n# Calculate the map distance\nmap_distance = (map_distance_per_10_miles / 10) * real_life_distance\n\n# Convert the map distance to a fraction\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nmap_distance_fraction = Fraction(map_distance).limit_denominator()\n\nprint(map_distance_fraction)\n```\n```output\n639/40\n```\nThe distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\\) inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the scale of the map and then use it to find the distance between the two buildings on the map in inches.\n\nThe scale of the map is given as 3 inches on the map equating to 10 miles in real life. This means that for every 10 miles in real life, the distance on the map is 3 inches. To find the distance on the map for 53.25 miles in real life, we can set up a proportion:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{x \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\r\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches\r\nreal_distance = 53.25  # miles\r\nscale_miles = 10  # miles\r\n\r\n# Calculate the map distance for 53.25 miles\r\nmap_distance = (map_distance_per_10_miles * real_distance) / scale_miles\r\nprint(map_distance)\n```\n```output\n15.975\n```\nThe distance between the two buildings on the map is \\(15.975\\) inches. To express this as a fraction, we recognize that \\(15.975\\) is equivalent to \\(\\frac{639}{40}\\).\n\nSo, the distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\\) inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to find the distance on the map that corresponds to 53.25 miles in real life, given that 3 inches on the map equates to 10 miles in real life.\n\nFirst, we need to find the scale of the map. The scale is the ratio of the distance on the map to the corresponding distance in real life. In this case, the scale is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Scale} = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nNow, we can use this scale to find the distance on the map that corresponds to 53.25 miles in real life. Let's denote the distance on the map as \\(d\\). The relationship is given by:\n\n\\[\nd = 53.25 \\text{ miles} \\times \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this expression to find \\(d\\):\n\n\\[\nd = 53.25 \\times \\frac{3}{10} = \\frac{53.25 \\times 3}{10}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this step by step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\