miles}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python.\n```python\n# Given values\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches\nreal_distance_per_10_miles = 10  # miles\nreal_distance = 53.25  # miles\n\n# Calculate the map distance\nmap_distance = (map_distance_per_10_miles / real_distance_per_10_miles) * real_distance\nmap_distance_fraction = map_distance\n\nprint(map_distance_fraction)\n```\n```output\n15.975\n```\nThe map distance corresponding to a real-life distance of 53.25 miles is 15.975 inches. To express this as a fraction, we recognize that 15.975 is the same as $\\frac{15975}{1000}$. We can simplify this fraction by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 15975 and 1000.\n\nThe GCD of 15975 and 1000 is 25. Dividing both the numerator and the denominator by 25, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15975 \\div 25}{1000 \\div 25} = \\frac{639}{40}\n\\]\n\nSo, the map distance is $\\frac{639}{40}$ inches.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\n\\]", "To solve the problem, we need to determine the distance between two buildings on the map given the real-life distance and the map's scale. The scale of the map is given as 3 inches on the map equating to 10 miles in real life. We need to find out how many inches on the map correspond to 53.25 miles in real life.\n\nWe can set up a proportion to solve this problem. Let's denote the distance on the map as \\(d\\) inches. The proportion can be written as:\n\\[\n\\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{d \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\nFrom this proportion, we can solve for \\(d\\):\n\\[\nd = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\nNow, let's calculate the value of \\(d\\).\n```python\n# Given values\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches\nreal_life_distance = 53.25  # miles\n\n# Calculate the map distance for 53.25 miles\nmap_distance = (map_distance_per_10_miles * real_life_distance) / 10\nprint(map_distance)\n```\n```output\n15.975\n```\nThe distance between the buildings on the map is \\(15.975\\) inches. To express this as a fraction, we need to convert \\(15.975\\) to a fraction. We can do this by recognizing that \\(15.975 = \\frac{15975}{1000}\\). Simplifying this fraction, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{15975}{1000} = \\frac{639}{40}\n\\]\nSo, the distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\frac{639}{40}\\) inches.\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\n\\]", "To solve the problem, we need to determine the map distance that corresponds to a real-life distance of 53.25 miles, given that 3 inches on the map equates to 10 miles in real life. We can set up a proportion to solve for the unknown map distance.\n\nLet's denote the map distance we are looking for as \\( x \\) inches. The proportion can be set up as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{x \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nFrom this proportion, we can solve for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nNow, let's calculate the value of \\( x \\) using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches\nreal_distance = 53.25  # miles\nreal_distance_per_10_miles = 10  # miles\n\n# Calculate the map distance for 53.25 miles\nmap_distance = (map_distance_per_10_miles / real_distance_per_10_miles) * real_distance\nprint(map_distance)\n```\n```output\n15.975\n```\nThe map distance corresponding to a real-life distance of 53.25 miles is \\( 15.975 \\) inches. To express this as a fraction, we recognize that \\( 15.975 \\) is equivalent to \\( \\frac{15975}{1000} \\). We can simplify this fraction by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 15975 and 1000.\n\nThe GCD of 15975 and 1000 is 25. Dividing both the numerator and the denominator by 25, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15975 \\div 25}{1000 \\div 25} = \\frac{639}{40}\n\\]\n\nSo, the distance between the buildings on 