air of equations:\n\\[\n2c - d = 3 \\quad \\text{(3)}\n\\]\n\\[\nc - 3d = -1 \\quad \\text{(4)}\n\\]\n\nFrom equation (4), we can express \\(c\\) in terms of \\(d\\):\n\\[\nc = 3d - 1.\n\\]\n\nSubstitute this into equation (3):\n\\[\n2(3d - 1) - d = 3 \\implies 6d - 2 - d = 3 \\implies 5d - 2 = 3 \\implies 5d = 5 \\implies d = 1.\n\\]\n\nThen, substitute \\(d = 1\\) back into the equation for \\(c\\):\n\\[\nc = 3(1) - 1 = 3 - 1 = 2.\n\\]\n\nSo, the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the image of the line \\(y = 2x + 1\\) under \\(\\mathbf{M}\\). Any point on the line \\(y = 2x + 1\\) can be written as \\((x, 2x + 1)\\). We need to find the image of this point under the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ 2x + 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ 2x + 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4x - (2x + 1) \\\\ 2x + (2x + 1) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2x - 1 \\\\ 4x + 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nSo, the image of the point \\((x, 2x + 1)\\) is \\((2x - 1, 4x + 1)\\). To find the equation of the line in the form \\(y = mx + b\\), we express \\(y\\) in terms of \\(x\\):\n\\[\ny = 4x + 1.\n\\]\n\nThus, the image of the line \\(y = 2x + 1\\) under \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) is \\(y = 4x + 1\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the matrix M\na, b, c, d = sp.symbols('a b c d')\nM = sp.Matrix([[a, b], [c, d]])\n\n# Define the equations based on the transformations\neq1 = sp.Eq(2*a - b, 9)\neq2 = sp.Eq(2*c - d, 3)\neq3 = sp.Eq(a - 3*b, 7)\neq4 = sp.Eq(c - 3*d, -1)\n\n# Solve the system of equations\nsolution = sp.solve((eq1, eq2, eq3, eq4), (a, b, c, d))\nM = M.subs(solution)\n\n# Define the line equation y = 2x + 1\nx = sp.symbols('x')\nline = sp.Matrix([x, 2*x + 1])\n\n# Find the image of the line under the matrix M\nimage = M * line\nimage_y = image[1].si