 gives us the system of equations:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{cases}\n   2a - b = 9 \\\\\n   2c - d = 3 \\\\\n   a - 3b = 7 \\\\\n   c - 3d = -1\n   \\end{cases}\n   \\]\n   Solving these equations, we get:\n   \\[\n   a = 4, \\quad b = -1, \\quad c = 2, \\quad d = 1\n   \\]\n   So, the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Transform the Line \\(y = 2x + 1\\):**\n   The line \\(y = 2x + 1\\) can be parameterized as \\(\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ 2x + 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\). We need to find the image of this line under the transformation by \\(\\mathbf{M}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ 2x + 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ 2x + 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4x - (2x + 1) \\\\ 2x + (2x + 1) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2x - 1 \\\\ 4x + 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n   \\]\n   Let \\(X = 2x - 1\\) and \\(Y = 4x + 1\\). We need to express \\(Y\\) in terms of \\(X\\):\n   \\[\n   X = 2x - 1 \\implies x = \\frac{X + 1}{2}\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\(x = \\frac{X + 1}{2}\\) into \\(Y = 4x + 1\\):\n   \\[\n   Y = 4 \\left( \\frac{X + 1}{2} \\right) + 1 = 2(X + 1) + 1 = 2X + 2 + 1 = 2X + 3\n   \\]\n   So, the image of the line \\(y = 2x + 1\\) under \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) is \\(Y = 2X + 3\\).\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{y = 2x + 3}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the matrix M\na, b, c, d = sp.symbols('a b c d')\nM = sp.Matrix([[a, b], [c, d]])\n\n# Define the equations based on the given transformations\neq1 = sp.Eq(2*a - b, 9)\neq2 = sp.Eq(2*c - d, 3)\neq3 = sp.Eq(a - 3*b, 7)\neq4 = sp.Eq(c - 3*d, -1)\n\n# Solve the system of equations\nsolution = sp.solve((eq1, eq2, eq3, eq4), (a, b, c, d))\nM = M.subs(solution)\n\n# Define the parameterized line\nx = sp.symbols('x')\nline = sp.Matrix([x, 2*x + 1])\n\n# Transform the line using matrix M\ntransformed_line =