e each term separately:\n\n1. For \\( \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\):\n   - Since \\( \\pi \\approx 3.14159 \\), \\( \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\approx 1.0472 \\).\n   - Since \\( \\frac{\\pi}{3} < 4 \\), we use \\( \\lceil \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\rceil \\).\n   - Therefore, \\( f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\lceil 1.0472 \\rceil = 2 \\).\n\n2. For \\( \\sqrt{45} \\):\n   - Since \\( 45 \\) is between \\( 36 \\) and \\( 49 \\), \\( \\sqrt{45} \\) is between \\( 6 \\) and \\( 7 \\). Specifically, \\( \\sqrt{45} \\approx 6.7082 \\).\n   - Since \\( \\sqrt{45} \\geq 4 \\), we use \\( \\lfloor \\sqrt{45} \\rfloor \\).\n   - Therefore, \\( f(\\sqrt{45}) = \\lfloor 6.7082 \\rfloor = 6 \\).\n\n3. For \\( 8^{2/3} \\):\n   - Since \\( 8^{2/3} = (2^3)^{2/3} = 2^2 = 4 \\), we have \\( 8^{2/3} = 4 \\).\n   - Since \\( 8^{2/3} = 4 \\geq 4 \\), we use \\( \\lfloor 8^{2/3} \\rfloor \\).\n   - Therefore, \\( f(8^{2/3}) = \\lfloor 4 \\rfloor = 4 \\).\n\nNow, we sum the results:\n\\[ f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) + f(\\sqrt{45}) + f(8^{2/3}) = 2 + 6 + 4 = 12 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Define the function f(n)\ndef f(n):\n    if n >= 4:\n        return math.floor(n)\n    else:\n        return math.ceil(n)\n\n# Calculate each term\nterm1 = f(math.pi / 3)\nterm2 = f(math.sqrt(45))\nterm3 = f(8 ** (2/3))\n\n# Sum the terms\nresult = term1 + term2 + term3\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).\n\nIn the Cartesian coordinate system, the coordinates of the point $\\left(2,-3\\right)$ with respect to the origin are ______.\nThe coordinates of the point \\((2, -3)\\) in the Cartesian coordinate system with respect to the origin are simply \\((2, -3)\\).\n\nLet's verify this using Python and the sympy library. We'll define the point and confirm its coordinates.\n\nHere is the Python code:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the point\nx, y = 2, -3\n\n# Coordinates of the point with respect to the origin\ncoordinates = 