 earned by Linda, Sherry, June, and Connie.\n2. Convert the total amount into cents.\n3. Determine how much money can be converted into dollar bills.\n4. Calculate the remaining amount in cents after converting as many coins into dollar bills as possible.\n\nLet's start by summing the total amount of money in dollars and then converting it into cents. We know that 1 dollar is equal to 100 cents. After converting the total amount into cents, we will then determine the remainder when divided by 100 to find out how many cents are left after converting as many coins into dollar bills as possible.\n\nHere is the Python code to perform these calculations:\n```python\n# Amounts earned by each person in dollars\nlinda_earned = 27.47\nsherry_earned = 35.23\njune_earned = 37.37\nconnie_earned = 26.52\n\n# Total amount earned in dollars\ntotal_dollars = linda_earned + sherry_earned + june_earned + connie_earned\n\n# Convert total amount to cents (1 dollar = 100 cents)\ntotal_cents = total_dollars * 100\n\n# Calculate the remainder when total_cents is divided by 100\nremaining_cents = total_cents % 100\n\nprint(remaining_cents)\n```\n```output\n59.00000000000074\n```\nAfter converting the total amount of money into cents and determining the remainder when divided by 100, we find that the remaining amount of money, in cents, after converting as many of the coins into dollar bills as they could is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{59}\n\\]", "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of money earned by all four girls.\n2. Convert the total amount into cents.\n3. Determine how many full dollar amounts can be taken out of the total amount in cents.\n4. Calculate the remaining cents after taking out the full dollar amounts.\n\nLet's break it down step-by-step and write the Python code to solve it.\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of money earned by all four girls.\n2. Convert the total amount into cents.\n3. Determine how many full dollar amounts can be t