\\]\n\nWe can set up the equations for the rows, columns, and diagonals:\n\n1. Sum of the first row: \\((n-3) + 3 + (n+1) = S\\)\n2. Sum of the second row: \\((n+2) + (2n-9) + 1 = S\\)\n3. Sum of the third row: \\(2 + n + (n-1) = S\\)\n4. Sum of the first column: \\((n-3) + (n+2) + 2 = S\\)\n5. Sum of the second column: \\(3 + (2n-9) + n = S\\)\n6. Sum of the third column: \\((n+1) + 1 + (n-1) = S\\)\n7. Sum of the main diagonal: \\((n-3) + (2n-9) + (n-1) = S\\)\n8. Sum of the other diagonal: \\((n+1) + (2n-9) + 2 = S\\)\n\nLet's solve these equations step-by-step using Python and sympy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nn = sp.symbols('n')\n\n# Define the common sum S\nS = sp.symbols('S')\n\n# Define the equations based on the rows, columns, and diagonals\neq1 = sp.Eq((n-3) + 3 + (n+1), S)\neq2 = sp.Eq((n+2) + (2n-9) + 1, S)\neq3 = sp.Eq(2 + n + (n-1), S)\neq4 = sp.Eq((n-3) + (n+2) + 2, S)\neq5 = sp.Eq(3 + (2n-9) + n, S)\neq6 = sp.Eq((n+1) + 1 + (n-1), S)\neq7 = sp.Eq((n-3) + (2n-9) + (n-1), S)\neq8 = sp.Eq((n+1) + (2n-9) + 2, S)\n\n# Solve the system of equations\nsolution = sp.solve([eq1, eq2, eq3, eq4, eq5, eq6, eq7, eq8], (n, S))\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\nSyntaxError: invalid syntax\n```\nIt looks like there was a syntax error in the code due to the way the equations were written. Specifically, the use of `2n` and `2n-9` without proper multiplication syntax caused the error. Let's correct the equations and solve them again.\n\nHere is the corrected code:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nn = sp.symbols('n')\n\n# Define the common sum S\nS = sp.symbols('S')\n\n# Define the equations based on the rows, columns, and diagonals\neq1 = sp.Eq((n-3) + 3 + (n+1), S)\neq2 = sp.Eq((n+2) + (2*n-9) + 1, S)\neq3 = sp.Eq(2 + n + (n-1), S)\neq4 = sp.Eq((n-3) + (n+2) + 2, S)\neq5 = sp.Eq(3 + (2*n-9) + n, S)\neq6 = sp.Eq((n+1) + 1 + (n-1), S)\neq7 = sp.Eq((n-3) + (2*n-9) + (n-1), S)\neq8 = sp.Eq((n+1) + (2*n-9) + 2, S)\n\