 the second row is:\n\\[ (n+2) + (2n-9) + 1 = 3n - 6 \\]\nSince this must also equal \\( S \\), we have:\n\\[ 3n - 6 = 2n + 1 \\]\nSolving for \\( n \\):\n\\[ 3n - 2n = 1 + 6 \\]\n\\[ n = 7 \\]\n\nWe can verify this value by checking the sums of the columns and the diagonals.\n\n3. The sum of the first column is:\n\\[ (n-3) + (n+2) + 2 = 2n + 1 \\]\nSince \\( n = 7 \\), this becomes:\n\\[ 2(7) + 1 = 15 \\]\n\n4. The sum of the second column is:\n\\[ 3 + (2n-9) + n = 3n - 6 \\]\nSince \\( n = 7 \\), this becomes:\n\\[ 3(7) - 6 = 15 \\]\n\n5. The sum of the third column is:\n\\[ (n+1) + 1 + (n-1) = 2n + 1 \\]\nSince \\( n = 7 \\), this becomes:\n\\[ 2(7) + 1 = 15 \\]\n\n6. The sum of the main diagonal is:\n\\[ (n-3) + (2n-9) + (n-1) = 4n - 13 \\]\nSince \\( n = 7 \\), this becomes:\n\\[ 4(7) - 13 = 28 - 13 = 15 \\]\n\n7. The sum of the other diagonal is:\n\\[ (n+1) + (2n-9) + 2 = 3n - 6 \\]\nSince \\( n = 7 \\), this becomes:\n\\[ 3(7) - 6 = 15 \\]\n\nSince all the sums are equal to 15, the value of \\( n \\) is indeed correct. Therefore, the value of \\( n \\) is \\( \\boxed{7} \\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the value of n\nn = 7\n\n# Define the magic square with the given n\nmagic_square = [\n    [n-3, 3, n+1],\n    [n+2, 2*n-9, 1],\n    [2, n, n-1]\n]\n\n# Calculate the sum of each row, column, and diagonal\nrow_sums = [sum(row) for row in magic_square]\ncolumn_sums = [sum(magic_square[i][j] for i in range(3)) for j in range(3)]\ndiagonal1_sum = sum(magic_square[i][i] for i in range(3))\ndiagonal2_sum = sum(magic_square[i][2-i] for i in range(3))\n\n# Check if all sums are equal\nall_sums = row_sums + column_sums + [diagonal1_sum, diagonal2_sum]\nis_magic_square = all(x == all_sums[0] for x in all_sums)\n\nprint((is_magic_square, n))\n```", "To solve this problem, we need to use the properties of a magic square. In a magic square, the sum of the numbers in each row, each column, and the two main diagonals is 