es of the equation to eliminate the square roots. This gives:\n\\[ y^2 = \\left( \\sqrt{x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}} + \\sqrt{x - \\sqrt{3x + 6}} \\right)^2. \\]\n3. Expand the right-hand side:\n\\[ y^2 = \\left( \\sqrt{x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}} \\right)^2 + \\left( \\sqrt{x - \\sqrt{3x + 6}} \\right)^2 + 2 \\sqrt{\\left( x + \\sqrt{3x + 6} \\right) \\left( x - \\sqrt{3x + 6} \\right)}. \\]\n4. Simplify the expression inside the square root:\n\\[ y^2 = x + \\sqrt{3x + 6} + x - \\sqrt{3x + 6} + 2 \\sqrt{x^2 - (3x + 6)}. \\]\n5. This simplifies to:\n\\[ y^2 = 2x + 2 \\sqrt{x^2 - 3x - 6}. \\]\n6. Since \\( y = 6 \\), we have:\n\\[ 36 = 2x + 2 \\sqrt{x^2 - 3x - 6}. \\]\n7. Divide both sides by 2:\n\\[ 18 = x + \\sqrt{x^2 - 3x - 6}. \\]\n8. Isolate the square root term:\n\\[ \\sqrt{x^2 - 3x - 6} = 18 - x. \\]\n9. Square both sides again to eliminate the square root:\n\\[ x^2 - 3x - 6 = (18 - x)^2. \\]\n10. Expand the right-hand side:\n\\[ x^2 - 3x - 6 = 324 - 36x + x^2. \\]\n11. Simplify and solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ -3x - 6 = 324 - 36x. \\]\n\\[ 33x = 330. \\]\n\\[ x = 10. \\]\n\nWe should verify that \\( x = 10 \\) satisfies the original equation. Let's substitute \\( x = 10 \\) back into the original equation and check:\n\n\\[ \\sqrt{10 + \\sqrt{3 \\cdot 10 + 6}} + \\sqrt{10 - \\sqrt{3 \\cdot 10 + 6}} = \\sqrt{10 + \\sqrt{36}} + \\sqrt{10 - \\sqrt{36}} = \\sqrt{10 + 6} + \\sqrt{10 - 6} = \\sqrt{16} + \\sqrt{4} = 4 + 2 = 6. \\]\n\nSince the left-hand side equals the right-hand side, \\( x = 10 \\) is indeed a solution. Therefore, the solution to the equation is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{10} \\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python code to ensure the accuracy.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = sp.symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the equation\r\nequation = sp.sqrt(x + sp.sqrt(3*x + 6)) + sp.sqrt(x - sp.sqrt(3*x + 6)) - 6\r\n\r\n# Solve the equation\r\nsolution = sp.solve(equation, x)\r\nprint(solution)\n```", "To solve the equation \\(\\sqrt{x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}} + \\sqrt